TI  - Harnessing AI and NLP for Enhanced Cybersecurity: A Strategic Approach to
      Mitigating Cybercrime
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - In the digital age, the complexity of cyber threats has escalated,
      necessitating more sophisticated cybersecurity approaches. Artificial
      Intelligence (AI) and Natural Language Processing (NLP) have become
      essential in strengthening cybersecurity measures, offering advanced
      capabilities in areas such as threat detection, predictive analysis, and
      defence against adversarial tactics. AI systems that integrate NLP are
      particularly effective at analysing large volumes of data, allowing them
      to identify and mitigate cyber threats in real-time. These technologies
      play a crucial role in detecting phishing schemes, forecasting potential
      cyberattacks, and countering adversarial activities. Nevertheless,
      incorporating AI and NLP into cybersecurity frameworks is not without its
      challenges, including concerns about data privacy, vulnerability to
      adversarial attacks, ethical issues, and substantial implementation costs.
      Despite these challenges, the future of cybersecurity is likely to be
      heavily shaped by developments in AI and NLP, with promising advancements
      anticipated in quantum-resistant AI, AI-supported human decision-making,
      and fully autonomous security systems. This paper delves into the role of
      AI and NLP in cybersecurity, examining their advantages, challenges, and
      potential future developments, while highlighting the importance of
      ongoing research and ethical considerations in the deployment of these
      technologies. We plan to conduct a comprehensive analysis of data
      collected from a range of published research papers. This in-depth
      examination will enhance our understanding and provide valuable insights
      into the subject matter, enabling us to draw more accurate and informed
      conclusions. © 2025 IEEE.
