AB  - The problem of algorithmic transparency is pressing. Predictive systems
      are transparent for consumers if they can ascertain the risks and benefits
      associated with the predictive systems to which they are subject. We
      examine three ways to meet this condition: disclosing source code,
      transparency without disclosing source code, and informational norms. ©
      2018 IEEE.
