AB  - Artificial intelligence in healthcare has the potential to enhance
      diagnostics, patient care, and medical research. However, trust in
      AI-driven decision-making processes is crucial as AI systems become more
      complex. Explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) is a strategy to ensure
      AI-driven healthcare solutions are efficient and understandable to
      healthcare professionals and patients. XAI can improve medical
      practitioners' decision-making processes, increase trust in AI
      recommendations, and boost patientdoctor communication. Applications
      include medical imaging, predictive analytics, drug development, and
      tailored treatment plans. The chapter discusses the ethical and regulatory
      implications of AI in healthcare, focusing on patient data privacy and
      security. Future XAI trends will focus on improving patient outcomes and
      healthcare service quality by making AI systems accessible and consistent
      with ethical norms. © 2024, IGI Global. All rights reserved.
