TI  - From Descriptive Insights to Autonomous Decisions: How AI and ML are
      Redefining Business Analytics
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) are revolutionizing
      business analytics by taking it beyond conventional static dashboards and
      descriptive reporting to more evolved predictive, prescriptive, and
      increasingly autonomous decision-making processes. This paper introduces a
      governance-infused analytics framework that incorporates reinforcement
      learning (RL), automated machine learning (AutoML), and natural language
      processing (NLP). We validate the proposed framework through two case
      studies: prescriptive process monitoring in the context of loan
      origination and the adoption of AutoML by small and medium enterprises
      (SMEs). The results demonstrate considerable improvements in conversion
      rates, operational efficiency, and adoption rates, while underlining the
      need for accountability mechanisms. In this context, we propose four
      governance metrics-Transparency Index, Bias Audit Score, Compliance
      Alignment Rate, and Robustness Score-that complement conventional
      performance metrics by integrating aspects of fairness, resilience, and
      compliance into AI-augmented decisionmaking systems. Finally, we outline
      three strategic imperatives, shifting from a model-centric to a
      systemoriented mindset, fostering human-in-loop co-learning, and
      establishing policy-driven AI, that will shape the next generation of
      business analytics. © 2025 IEEE.
