AB  - This chapter explores the transformative intersection of social commerce
      and machine learning in reshaping financial analysis and decision-making
      in the digital era. Social commerce, which blends social media interaction
      with e-commerce, has revolutionized consumer engagement and business
      strategies by integrating real-time communication, peer influence, and
      in-app transactions. Concurrently, machine learning offers powerful tools
      for predictive analytics, personalization, and automated financial
      statement analysis. The convergence of these domains presents new
      opportunities for real-time insights, customer-centric financial services,
      and dynamic business intelligence. This study employs a systematic review
      methodology guided by PRISMA standards to synthesize current literature,
      identify trends, and highlight ethical and operational challenges,
      including data privacy and algorithmic transparency. It emphasizes the
      growing impact of machine learning on enhancing the accuracy, efficiency,
      and responsiveness of financial analysis within the evolving landscape of
      social commerce. The chapter concludes by outlining future research
      directions and strategic implications for businesses aiming to thrive in
      this hybrid, data-driven environment. © 2026 by Apple Academic Press, Inc.
