TI  - Ethical AI in Energy: Addressing Data Privacy and Algorithmic Transparency
      in Smart Systems
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - This paper explores the integration of ethical AI in smart energy systems
      to ensure that data privacy and algorithmic transparency are evaluated.
      Leveraging advances in AI-driven energy management, including predictive
      analytics and grid optimization, the study addresses critical ethical
      challenges in data handling and decision-making processes. A mixed
      methodology combines qualitative reviews of 2022-2025 literature with
      quantitative assessments of privacy breaches and transparency metrics
      across 50 smart grid pilots. Results indicate a 12% reduction in privacy
      incidents with enhanced encryption and a 15% improvement in trust scores
      through transparent algorithms, validated by real-time X posts and web
      data. The discussion highlights the need for regulatory frameworks and
      user consent mechanisms, proposing a blueprint for ethical AI deployment.
      This work contributes to sustainable energy transitions by balancing
      innovation with ethical considerations, targeting net-zero goals by 2050.
      © 2025 IEEE.
