PB  - Springer Nature
AB  - Through better diagnosis accuracy, treatment plan optimization, and
      patient outcomes improvement, artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming
      world healthcare. Predictive analytics, deep learning applications,
      natural language processing (NLP), and robotic-assisted surgeries are
      among the newly developing artificial intelligence themes driving
      healthcare transformation investigated in this paper. Clinical
      decision-making is much advanced by the incorporation of artificial
      intelligence into automated disease detection, real-time monitoring, and
      tailored treatment. Furthermore changing patient care are AI-driven drug
      discovery and telemedicine technologies, thereby improving access to and
      efficiency of healthcare. Adoption of artificial intelligence in
      healthcare faces difficulties including data privacy issues, algorithmic
      bias, legislative restrictions, and the requirement of strong ethical
      frameworks notwithstanding its transforming power. This paper guarantees
      that AI-driven healthcare solutions are both efficient and fair by
      offering a thorough evaluation of these obstacles together with techniques
      to overcome them. Furthermore under discussion is how federated learning,
      explainable artificial intelligence, and AI-enabled electronic health
      records (EHRs) help to create a data-driven healthcare ecosystem. Through
      an analysis of present trends and future opportunities, this study
      emphasizes how important artificial intelligence is in forming the next
      generation of medical systems. For those working in healthcare,
      legislators, and artificial intelligence researchers trying to fully
      utilize AI for world healthcare transformation, the results provide
      insightful analysis. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer
      Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
