TI  - Explainable artificial intelligence (EAI): For healthcare applications and
      improvements
T2  - Explainable Artificial Intelligence for Biomedical and Healthcare
      Applications
SP  - 162-196
PY  - 2024
DA  - 2024
PB  - CRC Press
AB  - Explainable artificial intelligence (EAI) has emerged as a critical
      paradigm in the field of healthcare, offering unprecedented opportunities
      for enhancing patient care, diagnostic accuracy, and treatment outcomes.
      This abstract provides a concise overview of the significance and
      implications of EAI in healthcare applications and its potential to drive
      substantial improvements in the industry. In recent years, the integration
      of AI and machine learning techniques into healthcare systems has led to
      groundbreaking advancements in disease prediction, medical image analysis,
      drug discovery, and treatment personalization. However, the inherent
      opacity and complexity of many AI models have raised concerns regarding
      their trustworthiness and accountability in critical healthcare decisions.
      EAI addresses these concerns by providing transparent and interpretable AI
      models that not only deliver accurate predictions but also offer insights
      into the underlying decision-making processes. Here we discuss the
      multifaceted benefits of EAI in healthcare, including its ability to
      improve clinical decision support systems, enhance patient–doctor
      communication, and facilitate regulatory compliance. Furthermore, it
      explores various techniques and approaches employed in EAI, such as
      rule-based systems, feature importance analysis, and model-agnostic
      interpretability methods. These techniques empower healthcare
      professionals to understand AI-driven recommendations, validate their
      clinical relevance, and make informed decisions that align with the best
      interests of patients. The overview also sheds light on the challenges and
      future prospects of EAI in healthcare, emphasizing the need for
      standardized frameworks, data privacy safeguards, and continuous research
      to refine and expand the field. As the healthcare industry continues to
      harness the potential of AI, the adoption of EAI promises to bridge the
      gap between advanced technology and human expertise, ultimately leading to
      more effective, transparent, and accountable healthcare solutions. This
      abstract serves as an introduction to the pivotal role that explainable
      artificial intelligence plays in shaping the future of healthcare and
      highlights its potential to revolutionize patient care and medical
      research. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Aditya Khamparia and
      Deepak Gupta; individual chapters, the contributors.
