TI  - Hiring by Algorithms: The Role of AI in Recruitment and Selection with
      special reference to IT & Banking Sectors
SP  - 160-165
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Recruitment and
      Selection (R & S) has revolutionized hiring processes, particularly in
      Information Technology (IT) and Banking sectors by enhancing efficiency,
      reducing costs and minimizing human bias. AI driven tools such as
      Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), Machine Learning (ML) algorithms,
      Chatbots and predictive analytics streamline candidate screening, optimize
      talent acquisition and enable data driven hiring decisions. The IT sector
      has rapidly adopted AI to manage large applicant pools and assess
      technical competencies while the Banking sector leverages AI for mass
      recruitment, fraud detection and behavioral assessments. Despite its
      advantages, challenges like algorithmic bias, lack of transparency and
      data privacy concerns remain significant. This paper is an attempt to
      organise the existing studies, structure the relevant outcomes and
      understand the evolution, benefits and challenges of AI driven hiring,
      highlighting emerging trends such as explainable AI (XAI), ethical AI
      governance and AI powered digital interviews and finally suggest a human
      AI collaboration model to ensure fairness, diversity and effectiveness in
      hiring decisions. © 2025 IEEE.
SN  - 9798331537432
