TI  - MedTech Fusion in the Metaverse using business intelligence through
      AIoTBc: artificial intelligence, Internet of Things, blockchain
T2  - Healthcare Frontiers in the Metaverse: Innovations and Impacts
SP  - 19-54
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Elsevier
AB  - The Metaverse promises transformative advancements in healthcare delivery
      and patient outcomes. This chapter explores the integration of
      cutting-edge technologies Internet of Things (IoT), Federated Learning,
      Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI), and Blockchain into the
      Metaverse for the creation of ethical and efficient healthcare systems.
      The first section focuses on the general information regarding IoT and its
      capability for continuous health monitoring. The second section explores
      the advent of Federated Learning as a novel machine learning technique
      used to develop AI models that increase privacy in medical research and
      disease diagnosis. After this, this chapter turns to XAI, which
      demonstrates that through application within healthcare decision-making
      complex procedures can be made clear and easily understandable. Health
      data security is further discussed as a critical utilization of blockchain
      technology. Relating the findings to application, the practical
      implications are explained with examples. The second section gives
      practical cases on how smart inhalers are revolutionizing the management
      of chronic diseases, how Federated Learning applied to patient data can
      help detect early sepsis, how XAI makes patients understand the right
      therapy to be taken, and how Blockchain enhances patient records security.
      The following sections highlight the application of this knowledge within
      the context of medical education, to train healthcare professionals to
      understand better the Metaverse as well as to lead within the context of
      this new framework of healthcare delivery. It talks about ways by which
      the field shall be educated or trained on how to impart skills and
      knowledge to the concerned professions, resource allocation, and the
      inclusion of Metaverse as a medium for group learning rather than the
      conventional method of face-to-face. Finally, as a preview of what might
      come next in the field, the last but one section of the chapter outlines
      some of the future possibilities in using information technology like
      Predictive Analytics or Brain-Computer Interfaces in the healthcare
      sector. It builds on the importance of data ethics and systematic analysis
      in medical, training programs. The final part summarizes the main idea of
      the work, which is that it is necessary to apply technologies wisely and
      responsibly in the context of the Metaverse; the distributed system
      provided herein will supply quality healthcare to people and improve
      patient care without violating privacy and data protection at the same
      time. It requires establishing or developing a consistent healthcare
      system that focuses on flexibility and creativity to adapt to the changes
      in healthcare and include new technology. © 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights
      reserved.
