AB  - Machine learning is changing healthcare. This chapter highlights the risks
      for patients and the problems with models that are hard to understand. It
      explains how to make machine learning clear, using straightforward
      explanations and decision trees. Understanding these models is key to good
      decision-making in healthcare. It affects patient trust, follows the law,
      and ensures accountability. The research compares old “black-box” methods
      to transparent models. It uses real healthcare examples to show how they
      work. The chapter discusses the challenges of using these models and
      suggests how to integrate them into healthcare today. It emphasizes the
      importance of training healthcare workers and building trust. The
      conclusion looks ahead at what’s coming, ethical considerations, and
      advice for healthcare workers using machine learning. © 2026 selection and
      editorial matter, Dattatray G. Takale, Parikshit N. Mahalle, Sachin S.
      Bere, and Piyush P. Gawali; individual chapters, the contributors.
