AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence and predictive analytics with
      modern healthcare systems has improved the accuracy of clinical
      decision-making, resource management, and patient care delivery. The
      modern machine learning and deep learning techniques are used to design
      predictive models. These models process complex datasets acquired from
      electronic health records (EHRs), wearable devices, medical imaging, and
      real-time monitoring to extract features from hidden patterns and perform
      disease prediction. The healthcare staff achieve early diagnosis, optimize
      hospital operations, and reduce costs and improve the rate of patient
      satisfaction. The predictive analytics also supports precision medicine to
      provide personalized treatment strategies that reduce adverse drug
      reactions and enhance therapeutic efficacy. Although there are various
      advantages of AI-driven predictive analytics, there are several challenges
      to achieve the goal. There is risk of data privacy, algorithmic bias,
      interoperability, and ethical concerns. This paper presents a thorough
      review on AI-driven predictive analytics in healthcare, that highlights
      its applications, advantages, challenges, and emerging solutions such as
      explainable AI, federated learning, and reinforcement learning, which is
      essential for a sustainable, efficient, and patient-centred healthcare
      ecosystems. © 2025 IEEE.
