AB  - The adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) in law has the potential to
      fundamentally transform legal practice and processes, raising new
      questions about law, governance, and the delivery of justice, but the
      integration of AI into the legal system is consistently increased
      political sensitivity to accountability, transparency, and trust. This
      review explores the growing role of AI in the legal profession, examining
      the enabling technologies, social perspectives, potential benefits, and
      challenges. The study discusses how AI-powered tools are changing the
      balance of regulatory power, including predictive analytics and natural
      language processing capabilities Enabling more efficient but socially
      anxious data analysis and decision-making, sustaining impartiality,
      ensuring algorithmic transparency and accountability, and protecting
      client privacy and confidentiality. The paper argues that an updated
      regulatory framework and a flexible legal framework are needed to address
      the ethical aspects of AI in law. This study contributes to an ongoing
      dialogue on the implications of AI for the legal profession, highlighting
      the need for a nuanced understanding of the technology's impact on the
      foundations of justice and the pursuit of similar legal systems. © 2024
      IEEE.
