TI  - Artificial Intelligence for Business and Industry: A Strategic Framework
      for People Analytics in Human Resource Management
SP  - 196-201
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Artificial Intelligence has become deeply embedded in modern
      organizations, serving as a major driver of change. Among its many
      applications, People Analytics is one of the most impactful in Human
      Resource Management. Traditional methods and managerial instincts give way
      to AIenabled tools that offer more profound insight into workforce
      dynamics. Companies today use these tools to align talent strategy with
      business goals more accurately and effectively. Decision-making across the
      employee lifecycle is now faster and more precise. This shift is helping
      HR evolve into a strategic business partner rather than a supporting
      function. This paper takes a global and strategic view of how AI is being
      woven into core HR practices. It examines the influence of key
      technologies like machine learning, natural language processing (NLP), and
      predictive modeling on the various facets of HR. Practical insights and
      ethical issues are explored through real-world examples from companies
      such as Unilever, IBM, and Google. While AI brings many opportunities, it
      also raises concerns related to data privacy, fairness, and algorithmic
      transparency. The study presents a people-centered framework, offering
      guidance for organizations seeking to create more efficient, inclusive,
      and resilient workplaces. © 2025 IEEE.
