TI  - Explainable AI-Driven Business Process Optimization Using Hybrid
      Rule-Based and Deep Learning Algorithms
SP  - 1284-1291
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Business process optimization has become increasingly important for
      improving operational efficiency, regulatory compliance, and intelligent
      decision-making across modern enterprise environments. In this paper, we
      propose a novel Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI)-driven framework
      that combines rule-based expert systems with hybrid deep learning
      algorithms to optimize business processes while maintaining transparency,
      interpretability, and governance. The passiveaggressive emoji is a perfect
      expression of modern organizational dysfunction. In this paper, we propose
      a novel framework which combines Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI)
      with hybrid rule-based and deep learning algorithms to improve business
      process optimization. This thesis, therefore, aims to blend the
      deterministic accuracy of rulebased expert systems with humaninterpretable
      reasoning based on trained deep neural networks leading to a synergistic
      architecture which enforces predictive performance as well
      interpretability. The use of SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) and LIME
      (Local Interpretable Modelagnostic Explanations) ensures that every
      optimization decision is audit-ready, traceable, and compliant with domain
      business logic. The experimental evaluations performed in these three
      domains of supply chain management, customer service workflows and
      financial process automation all highlight significant efficiency gains
      with reductions in the cycle time of processes by up to 34% while
      maintaining a model interpretability score greater than 89%. This hybrid
      architecture closes the gap by providing stakeholders with an
      interpretable model that draws on black-box deep learning but also a
      transparent rule-based system, which makes it possible to trust and
      validate as well as refine recommendations given by an AI. With the
      introduction of this research, we provide a holistic and principled
      optimization pipeline that is both scalable and domain agnostic in nature,
      enabling enterprises to adopt intelligent automation solutions without
      compromising on governance, compliance or strategic accountability. © 2026
      IEEE.
