TI  - An XAI Framework for Heart Disease Oriented Healthcare Decision Support
      Systems
SP  - 813-819
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Heart disease continues to be one of the world's top causes of death,
      making sophisticated healthcare decision support systems necessary.
      Despite their effectiveness in prediction, traditional machine learning
      models frequently lack transparency, which prevents clinical use because
      of worries about accountability, bias, and reliability in high-stakes
      medical settings. In order to diagnose heart illness in clinical decision
      support systems (CDSS), this research suggests an Explainable Artificial
      Intelligence (XAI) framework. The approach concurrently improves
      predictive performance, model transparency, and clinical usability by
      combining inherently interpretable models, potent post-hoc explanation
      tools, and user-centred design principles. We provide a modular, scalable
      architecture that carefully strikes a compromise between explainability
      and diagnostic accuracy by combining ideas from recent developments in XAI
      for cardiovascular applications. Evaluations based on well-established
      benchmark datasets show high levels of physician satisfaction, great
      explanation quality, and enhanced diagnostic performance. This approach
      makes a significant contribution to closing the crucial gap between
      advanced AI-driven forecasts and realistic, evidence-based medical
      practice. © 2026 IEEE.
