AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) is fundamentally transforming cybersecurity,
      redefining how threats are detected, vulnerabilities are managed, and
      attacks are mitigated. By automating threat intelligence, enabling
      predictive analytics, and powering autonomous response systems, AI equips
      cybersecurity professionals with unprecedented capabilities. However, the
      integration of AI also introduces complex challenges, including
      adversarial attacks, explainability deficits, and ethical considerations.
      This chapter provides a comprehensive overview of how AI is reshaping the
      cybersecurity domain, drawing from recent advancements in threat
      detection, malware analysis, vulnerability prediction, autonomous defense,
      and offensive AI applications. It also evaluates governance and regulatory
      implications, offering strategic insights for security leaders and
      executive decision-makers. By weaving together real-world use cases,
      emerging trends, and open research challenges, the chapter serves as both
      a technical and strategic guide for navigating the next era of AI-driven
      cybersecurity. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under
      exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2027.
