TI  - Copyright, Privacy, and Ethical Issues of Generative AI
T2  - The Rise of Explainable and Generative AIDriven Cyber and Information
      Security
SP  - 81-111
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - IGI Global
AB  - Generative and explainable AI is rapidly transforming the cybersecurity
      and information security ecosystems through intelligent automation,
      adaptive threat detection, and decision support at unparalleled scale.
      While generative AI augments security operations by automating incident
      response, adversarial simulation, and threat intelligence synthesis, it
      simultaneously scales up cyber risks in deepfakes, polymorphic malware,
      and large- scale disinformation. This chapter critically discusses the
      dual- use nature of generative AI from a technical, legal, privacy,
      ethical, and governance perspective. Particular emphasis has been given to
      the pivotal role played by explainable AI in bringing accountability,
      legal defensibility, and human oversight back into automated security
      infrastructures. The chapter further reviews the global regulatory
      landscape, limitations in existing safeguards, and future research
      directions toward trustworthy, human- centered AI- enabled cybersecurity
      systems. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
