TI  - A Comprehensive Survey on AI-Enabled Physiotherapy: Advances in Human Pose
      Estimation, Exercise Assessment, and Personalized Tele-Rehabilitation
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in physiotherapy
      represents a paradigm shift toward accessible, scalable, and personalized
      rehabilitation care. This comprehensive survey systematically reviews the
      current state-of-the-art in AI-driven physiotherapy systems, focusing on
      human pose estimation, exercise recognition, movement quality assessment,
      and tele-rehabilitation platforms. We conducted a systematic literature
      review of 62 peer-reviewed studies published between 2019-2024, examining
      datasets, methodologies, evaluation metrics, and clinical validation
      approaches. Our analysis reveals significant advances in pose estimation
      accuracy (PCKh scores exceeding 97%), exercise recognition (F1-scores
      0.91), and quality assessment (R2 0.9 2). However, critical gaps persist
      in clinical validation, dataset diversity, real-world deployment, and
      explainable AI integration. We propose a novel taxonomy of AI
      physiotherapy systems categorizing approaches by sensing modality,
      processing architecture, and clinical application. Additionally, we
      present a comprehensive framework integrating multi-modal sensing,
      edge-cloud computing, and clinical decision support. Key research
      directions identified include federated learning for privacy preservation,
      multimodal foundation models, and clinically validated assessment
      frameworks. This survey provides researchers and practitioners with a
      comprehensive roadmap for developing next-generation AI physiotherapy
      solutions that bridge the gap between technical innovation and clinical
      implementation. © 2026 IEEE.
