TI  - A Neuro-Symbolic Agentic Framework for Personal Finance: Bridging
      Deterministic Logic with Generative Reasoning
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - In this paper, a neuro-symbolic agentic architecture of personalized
      financial decision support is proposed combining deterministic financial
      logic and generative reasoning. The system combines supervised machine
      learning models of goal classification and risk prediction with a
      controlled Large Language Model (LLM) to produce explanations. Synthetic
      data analysis has 89% and 85% accuracy on financial goal classification
      and risk appetite prediction respectively and good precision, recall and
      ROC-AUC. The architecture allows interpretability, auditability, and
      controlled reasoning and breaks significant weaknesses of the purely
      generative or purely rule-based systems. The suggested system stands a
      great chance of intelligent financial advisory systems that are accurate
      and scalable. © 2026 IEEE.
