TI  - Safe Cities and Smart Government for Transparency, Equity, and Resilience
T2  - Innovation, Transparency, and Participation in Smart Government
SP  - 179-224
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - IGI Global
AB  - This chapter critically explores the transformation of urban safety
      paradigms in response to accelerating urbanisation, complex systemic
      risks, and emerging technologies. It examines the integration of
      intelligent surveillance systems, predictive crime analytics, and advanced
      emergency management platforms, underpinned by artificial intelligence,
      the Internet of Things (IoT), and multisectoral data fusion. Emphasis is
      placed on the ethical and governance imperatives surrounding algorithmic
      transparency, digital equity, and cyber resilience. The analysis
      demonstrates that safe cities must move beyond reactive models towards
      anticipatory, inclusive frameworks that embed technological innovation
      within democratic, human- centred urban governance. The chapter concludes
      by identifying future challenges-including neuro- rights, post- quantum
      security, and digital exclusion-and advocates for a holistic, ethically
      grounded vision of urban resilience. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific
