TI  - Visualizing Autonomous Administration: Integrating Agentic AI With Higher
      Education Business Intelligence Architectures
T2  - Agentic AI and the Intelligent Transformation of Higher Education
SP  - 81-114
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - IGI Global
AB  - Higher education institutions increasingly operate through complex digital
      ecosystems in which student success, finance, research administration,
      human resources, and compliance depend on timely, explainable decisions.
      This chapter examines how agentic artificial intelligence can be
      integrated with business intelligence architectures to support autonomous
      administration without passing on institutional accountability. It
      proposes a layered reference architecture that combines data pipelines,
      semantic governance, visual analytics, process mining, human oversight,
      and policy-aware orchestration. The discussion connects learning
      analytics, explainable AI, and enterprise BI research to the realities of
      universities as mission-driven, high-stakes organizations. The chapter
      concludes with governance, implementation, and research recommendations
      for trustworthy, transparent, and resilient higher education
      administration across diverse institutional and regulatory contexts. ©
      2027 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
