TI  - AI-Powered Personalization Across Digital Ecosystems: A Trust-Centric
      Perspective on Intelligent, Ethical, and Adaptive User-Centric Systems
T2  - Appl. AI Lett.
JF  - Applied AI Letters
VL  - 7
IS  - 3
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - John Wiley and Sons Inc
AB  - Personalization based on Artificial Intelligence (AI) has become a
      paradigm shift in user-focused experiences in various digital ecosystems.
      We comprehensively and systematically discuss personalization methods
      through AI in the main domains including e-commerce, healthcare,
      education, entertainment, and finance. The current paper critically
      examines the basic techniques such as collaborative filtering,
      content-based filtering, hybrid recommendation methods, deep learning
      architectures, natural language processing (NLP), and reinforcement
      learning for their use in modeling complex user behavior and delivering
      personalized, context-aware recommendations. We propose a clear conceptual
      framework that visualizes the end-to-end personalization pipeline, from
      data collection to user profiling, training, real-time inference and
      feedback for optimization. Furthermore, the research uses mathematical
      concepts like a factorization of matrices and optimization methods to show
      how today's recommendation systems can be scaled and predicted. A
      real-world analysis is also explored, providing real-world benefits in
      user engagement, conversion rates and decision support systems. Besides
      technical improvements, this work also covers the key issues related to
      AI-based personalization, such as data privacy, security, bias in
      algorithms, and fairness. This study highlights the importance of the
      inclusion of ethical AI principles such as transparency, explainability,
      and user control in order to deploy AI responsibly. New trends such as
      explainable AI, cross-domain personalization and generative AI-based
      adaptive systems have also been explained, outlining the future of
      research. Overall, this research offers a holistic perspective, by
      bridging the technical meaning and ethical concerns, and offers valuable
      insights to the researchers, developers and industry practitioners aiming
      at designing scalable, intelligent and reliable personalization systems in
      future digital environments. © 2026 The Author(s). Applied AI Letters
      published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd.
