TI  - MediDiagnose: An Explainable AI-Powered Clinical Decision Support System
      Using Biomedical NLP and Human-in-the-Loop Validation
SP  - 197-202
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - We present MediDiagnose, a full-stack clinical decision support platform
      that integrates transformer-based biomedical NLP with explainable AI (XAI)
      and a human-in-theloop physician review workflow. The system accepts
      free-text symptom narratives and structured patient context, applies a
      fine-tuned BERT-family model to generate ranked differential diagnoses
      with confidence scores, and produces SHAP-derived word-importance
      explanations to justify each prediction. A state-machine-driven workflow
      enforces mandatory physician validation before any diagnosis is finalized,
      preserving clinical accountability. The architecture separates concerns
      across a React/Vite frontend, Node.js/Express API layer, MongoDB
      persistence tier, and an isolated Python inference subprocess.
      Experimental results demonstrate that the NLP pipeline achieves
      competitive disease-classification accuracy on the benchmark symptom
      dataset, while SHAP explanations significantly reduce physicians'
      uncertainty about accepting AI-assisted predictions. MediDiagnose
      demonstrates how modern biomedical NLP models can be responsibly embedded
      into end-to-end healthcare workflows that prioritize transparency,
      auditability, and physician governance. © 2026 IEEE.
