TI  - Cloud-Integrated Federated Machine Learning Framework for Prediction of
      Comorbidities in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus
SP  - 1027-1032
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - This review provides an overview of the design of a cloud-based federated
      machine learning architecture for the prediction of comorbid conditions of
      Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (T2DM). The key focus is on preserving patient
      data privacy, enhancing the ability to scale, enabling clinician
      interpretability of results while also integrating multi-factorial
      stratification of populations using factors such as age, sex, body mass
      index (BMI), and lifestyles. The combination of federated learning with
      both machine/deep learning architectures will enable simultaneous
      cross-institutional model training without compromising the privacy of
      individual patients' data. Techniques to provide explainable AI to enhance
      clinical decision-making via transparent predictive results are integrated
      into this review. This review will integrate recent advancements in T2DM
      comorbidity prediction, federated learning, and population-aware modeling
      to identify research gaps that have been identified and propose a unifying
      methodology to address these challenges. © 2026 IEEE.
