AB  - This study explores the emerging role of Grok, a novel AI language model
      developed by xAI, in addressing the complex challenges of water resource
      management (WRM). Through a review of the current literature on artificial
      intelligence applications in WRM and a comparative analysis with other
      large language models (LLMs), this paper assesses Grok's future potential
      in predictive modeling, water quality assessment, disaster monitoring, and
      policy support. Through the 10 key prompts created, this study evaluates
      Grok's potential capacity to enhance water treatment strategies, simplify
      scientific communication, engage stakeholders, and support climate
      resilience efforts. However, its reliance on unverified social media data
      risks biased outputs, while limited numerical modeling capabilities
      necessitate integration with specialized hydrological tools. © 2025 Policy
      Studies Organization.
