TI  - ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS IN AI-DRIVEN VIRAL MARKETING CAMPAIGNS
SP  - 78-86
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - The research investigates ethical problems that arise from using
      Artificial Intelligence (AI) in viral marketing campaigns through its
      systematic review of contemporary academic research. The researchers
      conducted their database search on ScienceDirect by using a structured
      search method that focused on the three primary search terms AI-driven
      marketing, viral marketing algorithms, consumer data privacy, and
      algorithmic bias. The study selected only peer-reviewed articles from the
      past five years because they needed recent and precise information. The
      study involved thematic analysis to identify and examine relevant sources
      from 50 final peer reviewed studies. The research demonstrates that AI
      improves marketing efficiency through personalized content, predictive
      analytics, and automated decision-making. However, it also creates serious
      ethical problems. The research identified four main problems that include
      consumer data protection issues, algorithmic transparency deficits, user
      behavior manipulation, and algorithmic bias that results in possible
      discrimination. The research demonstrates that AI-powered viral marketing
      increases risks because it spreads content quickly to an extensive
      audience. The research shows that organizations require solid ethical
      governance frameworks that need transparency together with responsible AI
      usage in their operations. Organizations need a framework that allows them
      to create new products which simultaneously upholds their ethical
      responsibilities, protects customer trust, and supports sustainable
      digital marketing practices. This study contributes to existing literature
      by providing a structured thematic synthesis of recent research, offering
      a comprehensive understanding of ethical risks and governance needs
      specific to AI-driven viral marketing. ©2026 IEEE.
