AB  - This chapter examines the role of Generative Artificial Intelligence
      (GenAI) in transforming modern marketing through automated content
      creation, predictive analytics, and personalized customer engagement. It
      highlights that the growing reliance on large-scale consumer data
      introduces concerns related to privacy, regulatory compliance, and ethical
      accountability. This chapter analyzes privacy-first frameworks and
      regulatory mechanisms for the responsible deployment of generative AI in
      marketing ecosystems. It discusses key global standards, including the ΕU
      AI Act, GDPR, and OΕCD AI Principles, alongside corporate responsible AI
      practices. Εthical risks such as data privacy violations, algorithmic
      bias, and lack of transparency are also examined, along with governance
      strategies including algorithmic auditing, explainable AI, and data
      governance. The chapter provides a structured foundation for developing
      ethical, transparent, and privacy-aware AI systems that support trust and
      sustainable innovation. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific
      Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without
      written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use
      of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI)
      technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to
      license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model
      development.
