TI  - From Data to Therapy: Artificial Intelligence Applications in
      Pharmacogenomics
T2  - Pharmacogenomics Using Artificial Intelligence: Optimizing Drug Response
      through Personalized Genomic Analysis
SP  - 23-48
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - wiley
AB  - Pharmacogenomics (PGx) research has created a new foundational knowledge
      for understanding the impact of genetic variation on drug response, about
      which we are beginning to slowly evolve toward personalized medicine.
      Nevertheless, the complexities, amounts, and variability of multi-omics
      and clinical data will always be challenges and will continue to challenge
      the application of gained genomic knowledge to therapeutic interventions
      and clinical contexts. However, artificial intelligence (AI) is a powerful
      tool that can help facilitate, integrate, compare, analyze, and interpret
      incoming datasets with the objective of predicting drug efficacy,
      optimizing dosing, and ultimately enhancing the reduction of adverse drug
      reactions, safety, and efficacy in real time. In this article, we will
      review and impersonalize the existing body of AI methods currently applied
      in PGx, including machine learning, deep learning, natural language
      processing, and graphbased methods used to convert a wide range of varied,
      raw genomic datasets into relevant and useful strategies for treatment.
      This will involve our quantification of examples of real-world
      applications across therapeutic areas, addressing some barriers to
      AI-driven PGx (e.g., data privacy, algorithmic bias, interpretability),
      and provide a synthesis of the promising next steps in this space (i.e.,
      advancements in explainable AI, federated learning, potential use of
      Internet of Things devices to obtain real-world data in real time in PGx).
      AI-assisted PGx can bridge the gap from genomic scientists to clinicians
      and streamline the movement along the data-to-therapy continuum across the
      entire patient experience in healthcare and performance-creating the next
      chapters in the evolution toward precision and personalized medicine. ©
      2026 Scrivener Publishing LLC.
