AB  - Dermatological diseases are among the most common health issues worldwide,
      and early detection is vital for effective treatment. This study proposes
      a hybrid CNN framework with transfer learning for advanced dermatological
      image analysis. By combining pre-trained models such as ResNet and
      Efficient Net, the system enhances feature extraction and classification
      performance. Confidence thresholding is employed to ensure high
      reliability predictions, while Bayesian CNNs provide uncertainty
      estimation. To preserve data privacy, federated learning enables
      collaborative training without sharing patient information. Additionally,
      explainable AI (XAI) techniques highlight critical image regions
      influencing the model's decisions, improving clinical interpretability.
      The proposed framework enhances diagnostic accuracy, reliability, and
      transparency, making it a promising AI-driven decision-support tool for
      dermatology. © 2026 IEEE.
