TI  - Explainable artificial intelligence in healthcare: Transparency and
      trustworthiness
T2  - Artificial Intelligence and Cybersecurity in Healthcare Cyber Physical
      Systems
SP  - 243-272
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - John Wiley and Sons Inc.
AB  - This chapter explores the growing importance of Explainable Artificial
      Intelligence (XAI) in healthcare, focusing on its role in enhancing
      transparency and fostering trust in AI-powered medical tools. As AI
      increasingly impacts diagnostics, treatment planning, and patient
      outcomes, the ability to understand and interpret AI decisions is
      critical. The chapter highlights various XAI methodologies that make
      complex models, such as deep learning, more interpretable for clinicians,
      patients, and stakeholders. It also examines real-world examples where XAI
      has improved clarity in AI-driven healthcare applications, ensuring that
      AI systems are not only accurate but also offer clear explanations behind
      their decisions. Ethical considerations, including the need for fairness,
      accountability, and patient safety, are discussed in detail, alongside the
      challenges of implementing XAI in clinical environments. By addressing
      these issues, this chapter underscores the transformative potential of XAI
      in building trust and ensuring responsible AI use in healthcare, while
      maintaining human oversight and ethical responsibility. © 2025 Scrivener
      Publishing LLC. All rights reserved.
