TI  - From Algorithms to Heartbeats: A Survey of AI and IoT Approaches in Heart
      Disease Prediction
SP  - 106-111
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Cardiovascular disease is one of the leading causes of morbidity and
      mortality globally, without regard to geography or social status.
      Advancements in Internet of Things (IoT) as well as artificial
      intelligence (AI) have opened up new avenues of proactive cardiovascular
      care especially in the space of early detection continuous monitoring as
      well as risk assessment. In this review, we collect and analyze current AI
      and IoT based heart disease prediction frameworks, with an emphasis onto
      the endeavors to translate from the lab to the clinic. The state of the
      art is reviewed in terms of approaches from traditional machine learning,
      deep learning architectures, and wearable sensorbased systems as well as
      their potential in decision support and patient management. From a
      technical and clinical perspective, practical issues of data security and
      privacy, algorithms transparency and integration with the existing
      healthcare workflows are explored. To aid in developing the field,
      datasets, evaluation metrics and typologies of methods are summarized as a
      reference. The review also highlights research gaps and new directions of
      work that might contribute to more trustworthy, personalized and ethically
      sensitive intelligent systems in cardiovascular health care. © 2026 IEEE.
