AB  - Integrating artificial intelligence (AI) in emergency medical (EM) has
      been proven to be transformative by improving specific key performance
      indicators (KPIs) such as patient wait times, treatment accuracy, and
      resource allocation to enhance performance efficiency and clinical
      outcomes. This paper examines the application of AI in EM with a focus on
      KPIs. AI features such as predictive analytics and machine learning
      increase patient flow, enhance staff productivity, and reduce waiting
      time. Moreover, AI utilization is limited by several factors, including
      data privacy concerns, Lack and scarcity of transparency in
      decision-making, and regulatory barriers. This paper addresses these
      barriers to the future use of AI in EM and healthcare, focusing on the
      importance of model interpretability, data standardization, and adaptive
      regulatory frameworks. The focus is on integrating AI to increase
      efficiency, improve outcomes, and optimize the use of resources in
      emergency healthcare. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer
      Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
