AB  - The rapid adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) in healthcare has
      enabled intelligent diagnostics, personalized treatment, and real-time
      clinical decision support. However, these advancements also introduce
      significant challenges related to data privacy, cybersecurity, and secure
      software deployment. Healthcare AI systems operate on highly sensitive
      patient data and are increasingly targeted by cyber threats, including
      data breaches, ransomware attacks, and adversarial manipulation of machine
      learning models. This chapter presents a comprehensive exploration of
      privacy-preserving and secure AI-driven healthcare systems, emphasizing
      the integration of federated learning, explainable AI, and
      quantum-resilient cybersecurity mechanisms. The chapter examines secure
      software architectures and collaborative AI frameworks that enable
      effective interaction between intelligent systems and healthcare
      professionals while maintaining regulatory compliance and ethical
      integrity. © 2027 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights
      reserved.
