AB  - Process Sentience has been introduced as a higher order of Autonomous
      Business Process Management whereby workflows become more dynamic, instead
      of being rule-based automation, and cognitively coordinated and
      governance-conscious systems. The response to real-time cues and risk
      response is achieved through dynamic reconfiguration of processes using
      structured Cognitive-Orchestration Framework of sensing, reasoning,
      learning, and adaptive action. Evidence of cross-domain proves that there
      are measurable improvements in resilience, efficiency, accuracy, and
      compliance. Autonomy gradients guarantee calibrated autonomy aided by
      transparency, auditability and human monitoring, making BPM a strategic
      ability in intelligent these days firms. © 2027 by IGI Global Scientific
      Publishing. All rights reserved.
