TI  - Exploring Cloud Security in Medical Sciences Through Machine Learning: A
      Systematic Literature Review
VL  - 1
SP  - 1995-2004
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Grenze Scientific Society
AB  - With the Health care system moving towards cloud systems, protecting such
      sensitive health data from security threats have become very crucial. The
      present study aims at studying the effectiveness of ML techniques in
      improving the security of the cloud from the field of medical sciences. As
      most of the healthcare firms opt for cloud solutions for processing and
      managing personal health information, protection of such data from leakage
      or other forms of invasion poses a very serious problem. Much of cloud
      security research focuses on problems that are common in the medical
      sciences domain, such as, data confidentiality, authorization, and anomaly
      detection. This includes the way in which the following advanced ML
      methodologies were used to solve these challenges, including encryption
      algorithms, anomalous detection systems, and predictive analysis. What the
      research has shown include examining ML techniques that have been used, as
      detailed in the literature and an assessment of the associated
      improvements to cloud security measures. This paper has found out that
      there are major positive impacts that flow from the usage of Machine
      Learning algorithms in the protection in the Healthcare data as much as
      there has been a lot of progress regarding the protection of HC data using
      ML algorithms, there are challenges, including the black-box kind of
      models that are hard to understand and the lack of identifiable solution
      deployment frameworks. The work ends with a discussion of the current
      limitations: the models' non-interpretable nature and variations in model
      performance in different care settings. Several research avenues and
      recommendations for further studies are discussed; the study proposes the
      focus on constructive development of explainable AI models, creation of
      best practices and standards, and the search for new opportunities with
      the help of innovative technologies to improve cloud security in the field
      of medical sciences. Thus, the findings of this research provide insights
      about integrating ML into cloud security and provide a direction for
      research in this emerging domain. © Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.
