TI  - Role of AI in gastroenterology: Prevention, diagnostics, and treatment
T2  - Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Sciences and Healthcare
SP  - 99-115
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - CRC Press
AB  - The application of artificial intelligence (AI) in gastroenterology has
      demonstrated transformative potential, improving diagnostic accuracy,
      enhancing therapeutic outcomes, and personalizing patient care. This study
      explores various domains within gastroenterology where AI is being
      integrated, including endoscopic advancements, disease prediction, and
      management, as well as the processing of large-scale healthcare data. We
      systematically review current AI technologies such as machine learning
      algorithms and deep learning frameworks applied to gastrointestinal
      imaging, pathology, and genomics. The accuracy of AI systems in detecting
      and diagnosing conditions such as colorectal cancer, gastroesophageal
      reflux disease, and inflammatory bowel disease, among others, is
      highlighted through comparisons with traditional diagnostic methods.
      Furthermore, the study delves into the role of AI in improving the
      efficiency of endoscopic procedures through automated lesion detection,
      characterization, and even robotic assistance. Challenges pertaining to AI
      integration in clinical practice are discussed, including data privacy,
      algorithmic transparency, need for robust validation frameworks, and the
      necessity of interdisciplinary collaboration to ensure ethical deployment.
      Future perspectives focus on potential innovations and the expansion of AI
      applications into personalized treatment plans and real-time decision
      support systems. The study concludes with recommendations for overcoming
      current barriers and enhancing the symbiosis between AI technologies and
      gastroenterological healthcare practices. © 2026 selection and editorial
      matter, Imran Khan and Santosh Kumar.
