AB  - Aim: Integrating artificial intelligence (AI) into workplace functioning
      is revolutionizing the way organizations enable employee wellness,
      work-life balance, and mental health. Predictive models and
      health-monitoring systems create opportunities for proactive interventions
      designed to result in healthier, more sustainable workplaces. Need for the
      study: This chapter highlights Al's growing role in promoting employee
      wellness through work-life balance, stress management, and mental health -
      and forms the basis of the study at hand. It looks at predictive AI models
      and health-monitoring systems that use biometric and wearable data to
      facilitate real-time insights, averting issues such as burnout. Method:
      This conceptual paper synthesizes literature and theory to illustrate the
      role of AI tools such as predictive algorithms and healthmonitoring
      systems in employee wellness, work-life balance, and mental health
      support. Findings: There are both apps and devices that have advantages
      (such as virtual reality to Repose) and Al-generated health-monitoring
      tools. It emphasizes ethical issues surrounding AI deployment, such as the
      need for transparency via explainable AI (XAI). These innovations are
      changing the workplace landscape to nurture employee wellness and mental
      health, thus enabling a good future of work that is balanced and
      sustainable. Causes and practical implications: AI tools improve work-life
      balance, reduce burnout, and promote engagement increase wellness.
      Wearables and predictive analytics now provide real-time health insights
      while customized wellness initiatives become tailored to consumers. AI
      chatbots facilitate wellness resource access. Ethical considerations such
      as data privacy and transparency are essential for building trust and
      achieving long-term success. © 2025 by Tanusree Chakraborty, V. S. Sharada
      and Sarthak Sengupta. All rights reserved.
