TI  - Risk, Regulation, and AI: Strengthening Financial Integrity in SAP S/4HANA
      Workflows
VL  - 2025 LNNS
SP  - 364-375
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH
AB  - The issue of financial integrity is also critical in the contemporary
      business since there is an increased risk in the regulatory investigations
      of organizations, more intricate compliance systems, and even increased
      fraud and misreporting. As companies adopt the use of SAP S/4HANA as an
      intelligent enterprise resource planning (ERP) system, companies are
      revising workflow models with a view to making them transparent,
      accountable, and regulatory compliant. Provided in this paper, the topic
      of artificial intelligence (AI) implementation in SAP S/4HANA operations
      is touched upon as a way of enhancing financial integrity and reducing
      risks along with facilitating regulatory compliance. Using a literature
      analysis on the topic, we are examining the ways in which the standard
      financial controls are being revolutionized by AI driven automation,
      detection of anomalies and predictive analytics. A methodology framework
      is provided to analyze the risk-sensitive processes of accounts payable,
      revenue recognition, audit trial management. The findings point to the
      possible advantages of AI-based SAP S/4HANA named the possibility to
      minimize manual error, increase fraud detection, and accuracy of
      compliance reporting. The discussion focuses on the proportion between
      technological opportunities and challenges, especially in the data
      governance, explanation of the meaning of AI decisions, and legality, and
      whether these changes and regulations are accepted. Although the process
      of AI integration has enormous potential advantage, effective drawbacks
      are high cost, organizational resistance to change, and the complexity of
      its association to new financial laws. Future studies should aim at
      creating explainable AI solutions, scalable governance frameworks and
      industry specific compliance templates which would be consistent across
      the global and local regulatory landscape. © The Author(s), under
      exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
