AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into clinical research and
      precision medicine has been rapid and has revolutionized the data-driven
      innovation in the healthcare space. However, the growing dependence on
      complex machine learning
      anddeeplearningmodelshasraisedseriousconcernsaboutthelackoftransparency,
      interpretability and trust in the models. Black-box AI systems can also
      limit clinician confidence, make it very difficult to get systems approved
      by regulators, and create tensions at the patient-facing decision-making
      level. This chapter examines the establishment and how to employ
      Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) platforms adaptively towards
      clinicalresearchecosystem and precision medicine applications. It offers a
      day-to-day structured multi-layer design fitting data governance,
      predictive models, explainability engines and human in-the-loop validation
      mechanism. Special emphasis is placed on artificial intelligence-based
      patient recruitment; risk stratification; treatment individualisation;
      clinical decision support systems. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific
      Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without
      written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use
      of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI)
      technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to
      license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model
      development.
