TI  - Resilient and sustainable supply chains: Leveraging AI and IoT for
      real-time risk intelligence
T2  - Artificial Intelligence for Sustainable Supply Chain Management
SP  - 127-158
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - CRC Press
AB  - Modern supply chains face growing uncertainties from climate change,
      geopolitical tensions, and pandemics, demanding not just efficiency but
      resilience. This chapter explores how the synergy of artificial
      intelligence (AI) and the Internet of Things (IoT) empowers real-time risk
      detection, mitigation, and adaptive decision-making in sustainable supply
      chain ecosystems. It introduces an integrated AI–IoT framework that
      enhances visibility, responsiveness, and sustainability through predictive
      analytics, sensor-driven monitoring, and dynamic resource allocation.
      Real-world case studies spanning agriculture, healthcare logistics, and
      manufacturing illustrate the impact: reduction in spoilage by up to 40% in
      perishable goods logistics, 30% fewer machine breakdowns through
      predictive maintenance, and up to 25% optimization of delivery routes that
      reduce fuel use. These intelligent automation strategies minimize
      disruptions, reduce emissions, and support circular supply models.
      Furthermore, the chapter addresses ethical deployment challenges,
      including data privacy, bias in AI models, and the necessity of
      explainable AI. By integrating both technological and socio-environmental
      dimensions, this work offers a strategic roadmap for designing resilient,
      responsible, and sustainable supply chains. © 2026 selection and editorial
      matter, N. Nasurudeen Ahamed, P. Karthikeyan and Polinpapilinho F. Katina;
      individual chapters, the contributors.
