AU  - Menaka, D
AU  - Subhashini, K S
AU  - Kalyani, S
AD  - Department of ECE, Sri Venkateswara College of Engineering, Sriperumbudur,
      India
TI  - The Integration of IoT and Machine Learning in Healthcare
T2  - Harnessing the Power of IoT-Enabled Machine Learning in Healthcare
      Applications
SP  - 51-81
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Nova Science Publishers, Inc.
AB  - The healthcare industry could undergo a significant transformation as a
      result of the confluence of machine learning (ML) and internet of things
      (IoT) technology. This could lead to proactive and individualized patient
      care, effective resource allocation, and data-driven. While IoT is
      involved in the gathering of resources and data, ML approaches handle data
      analysis, data expansion, learning, and decision-making based on input
      data. Combining these two technologies can greatly benefit the clinical
      sector by creating an environment that is responsive and interconnected,
      which will benefit patients and healthcare workers by offering a variety
      of services. The creation of smart apps for medical applications, such as
      wearable modules, smart capsules, and sensorybased units to assist medical
      professionals in gathering data, form the basis of IoT devices. By
      assessing and identifying multiple variances in a patient's health state,
      ML models can offer alternate diagnosis procedures and ultimately enhance
      the patient's health outcome. This chapter explores the integration of ML
      algorithms with IoT devices in healthcare contexts, highlighting the
      symbiotic link between these two paradigms. It delves into the various
      applications of ML in processing vast streams of IoT-generated healthcare
      data, including predictive analytics for disease diagnosis, anomaly
      detection for remote patient monitoring, and optimization of healthcare
      operations. The Internet of Medical Things (IoMT) is a next-generation
      bioanalytical tool that integrates network-linked biomedical devices with
      a software application to improve human health, emerging in the same age.
      In this chapter, the role of AI and IoMT in enhancing the functionality,
      detection precision, decision-making capability, and assessment of related
      hazards created for cutting-edge biomedical applications are also
      addressed. Thus it provides insights into the revolutionary potential of
      merging ML and IoT to reform healthcare delivery and enhance patient
      outcomes through real-world case studies and future prospects. A detailed
      comparative analysis of various methodologies in terms of advantages,
      challenges and applications has been addressed which will aid healthcare
      practitioners, and future researchers by providing insightful information
      about recent developments in smart healthcare. Furthermore, the challenges
      and opportunities inherent in this integration, such as ensuring data
      privacy and security, addressing interoperability issues, and fostering
      collaboration among stakeholders are examined. In summary, the application
      of IoT and ML in healthcare has a great potential as it can incorporate
      novel methods such as explainable AI, federated learning, and
      context-aware health monitoring systems which will enhance the system's
      responsiveness, accuracy, and patient-centeredness, ultimately leading to
      better patient outcomes and care quality. © 2025 Nova Science Publishers,
      Inc. All rights reserved.
