AB  - The use of Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) in Data-Driven
      Decision Support Systems (DSS) is a paramount development in several
      fields of work, such as healthcare, finance, or engineering. XAI aims at
      making AI models transparent, interpretable and understandable to human
      users so that any decision-making process that is fuelled by AI can be
      trusted and explained. The paper explores the use of XAI in improving the
      reliability, transparency and accountability of DSS. Based on the
      examination of the current methods and models, we come up with a holistic
      methodology to incorporate XAI methods to DSS, with a focus on the
      trade-off between model accuracy and interpretability. The effectiveness
      of the proposed approach is demonstrated with the help of a case study of
      a predictive healthcare system. The results indicate the urgency of
      explainability in AI-based decision support, and the framework suggested
      can increase the acceptance of the use of AI and compliance with the
      regulations. © 2026 IEEE.
