AD  - Saveetha University, SIMATS, Saveetha School of Law, Tamil Nadu, Chennai,
      India
TI  - Explainable AI for Transparent Legal Decision Support in Judicial Systems
      Using Hybrid LegalTech Framework
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - This study introduces a hybrid Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI)
      framework to improve transparency, accountability, and reliability in
      legal decision support systems. The framework combines rule-based legal
      reasoning with data-driven models, integrating Random Forest classifiers
      with Legal-BERT embeddings to capture both structured statutory signals
      and nuanced semantic patterns in judicial texts. Evaluated on a curated
      dataset of 35,000 Indian High Court judgments, the proposed approach
      achieved 94.8% accuracy, 93.5% precision, and 95.1% recall, representing
      an 11% relative improvement over standalone baselines. The dataset was
      collected from publicly available Indian High Court digital repositories
      and underwent extensive preprocessing including anonymization, text
      normalization, and removal of redundant metadata to ensure ethical use and
      consistency in analysis. Explainability is provided through SHAP value
      analysis and attention visualizations that expose feature contributions,
      legal citations, and contextual phrases that influence predictions. An
      ablation study demonstrates the contribution of the rule-based layer to
      interpretability with minimal performance trade-offs. A user evaluation
      with legal professionals yielded an average interpretability score of
      4.5/5, indicating practical acceptability. The framework aims to bridge
      data-driven inference and principled legal reasoning, supporting judicial
      workflows without supplanting human judgment. Future study will extend
      evaluation across multi-jurisdictional datasets and implement
      privacy-aware data governance to ensure ethical deployment in operational
      settings. Comprehensive documentation, reproducible code, and deployment
      guidelines are provided to facilitate transparent adoption widely by
      practitioners and stakeholders. © 2025 IEEE.
