TI  - Artificial Intelligence in Accounting and Finance: A Systematic Review of
      Emerging Technologies and Practical
SP  - 518-523
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Accounting and finance are being fundamentally transformed by Artificial
      Intelligence (AI): intelligent automation, sophisticated analytics, and
      data-driven decisions can be achieved. Conventional financial systems,
      which have long relied on manual approaches and rule-based solutions, are
      undergoing more and more additions of Machine Learning, Deep Learning,
      Natural Language Processing, and Robotic Process Automation. The
      technologies are in support of automated bookkeeping, intelligent
      auditing, fraud detection, credit risk modeling, portfolio optimization,
      and financial forecasting. AI systems enhance efficiency, accuracy, and
      realtime generation of insights after analyzing large volumes of
      structured and unstructured financial data. The current review paper is a
      systematic study of recent advances in accounting and finance of AI use,
      where methods are divided into categories, and key practical applications
      are identified. It also examines the latest trends, such as explainable
      AI, financial reporting using generative AI, and systems that are powered
      by AI and support decision-making. In spite of major improvements, issues
      can still be encountered regarding the interpretability of the model,
      regulatory compliance, data privacy, ethical aspects, and the risk of
      cybersecurity. The paper proposes research gaps that are critical and maps
      the directions in the future to facilitate transparent, reliable, and
      scalable intelligent financial systems that add to the research in
      academia and industry practice. © 2026 IEEE.
