AU  - Sayles, R
AU  - Alsharari, N M
AD  - Comcast Business, United States
TI  - Revolutionizing Financial Operations: AI in Telecommunications Accounting
T2  - AI in Accounting: Leveraging Artificial Intelligence to Transform
      Accounting Practices
SP  - 255-269
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Emerald Publishing
AB  - This chapter investigates the transformative impact of artificial
      intelligence (AI) on accounting practices within the telecommunications
      industry, with a particular focus on two major players: Comcast and
      T-Mobile. As these companies manage vast volumes of financial transactions
      and operate in a highly dynamic, data-intensive environment, the
      integration of AI technologies has become essential for maintaining
      operational efficiency, financial accuracy, and strategic agility. This
      chapter explores how AI is being leveraged to automate routine accounting
      tasks, enhance fraud detection mechanisms, improve financial forecasting,
      ensure regulatory compliance, and support strategic financial planning.
      Through case study analysis and data visualization, this chapter provides
      a comprehensive examination of AI’s role in reshaping accounting
      functions. It highlights how machine learning algorithms, robotic process
      automation (RPA), and predictive analytics are being deployed to
      streamline processes, reduce human error, and generate actionable insights
      from complex datasets. The case studies of Comcast and T-Mobile illustrate
      real-world implementations of these technologies, showcasing both the
      measurable benefits and the operational challenges encountered during
      adoption. This chapter addresses broader implications of AI integration,
      including ethical considerations, data governance, and the evolving role
      of accounting professionals. Issues such as algorithmic transparency, bias
      in financial decision-making, and the need for upskilling the workforce
      are critically examined. The discussion is contextualized within the
      broader landscape of digital transformation in the telecommunications
      sector, offering insights into how AI is not only enhancing accounting
      efficiency but also contributing to strategic competitiveness. © 2026 Hala
      Zaidan, Yaser Allozi and Ra’ed Masa’deh. Individual chapters © 2026 The
      authors.
