TI  - A Multi-Agent System for Equity Analysis
SP  - 391-396
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery, Inc
AB  - Financial markets produce large volumes of heterogeneous data that must be
      synthesized to inform investment decisions and risk evaluation.
      Conventional machine learning models offer strong predictive performance
      but demand programming expertise and lack natural-language interactivity,
      while large language models provide fluent communication yet cannot
      independently perform numerical simulations or scenario-based reasoning.
      This paper introduces a multi-agent architecture that unifies analytical
      AI and generative AI to support equity analysis. The system is
      orchestrated by a Manager Agent and includes six specialized agents: a
      Chat Agent for conversational interaction, a Text-to-SQL Agent enabling
      natural-language access to structured databases, an Unstructured Data
      Agent for document retrieval, an ML/SHAP Agent for explainable
      stock-movement prediction, a Visualization Agent for generating
      decision-support plots, and a Scenario Analysis Agent for simulating
      perturbed market conditions. Through a unified natural-language interface,
      the system integrates structured market data with unstructured financial
      documents. Experiments on Vietnam stock market data (January 2024-August
      2025) show strong performance across components: the Text-to-SQL agent
      achieves 90% validity on complex queries with iterative correction, the
      Unstructured Data agent attains 91.9% accuracy on document-grounded
      questions, and ML outputs align 100% with manual benchmarks. The proposed
      architecture accelerates analytical workflows while ensuring transparency
      and auditability, offering a practical foundation for deploying
      multi-agent AI systems in emerging market equity research and providing
      pathways for future extensions in trading, risk management, and compliance
      applications. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
