TI  - Elucidable Artificial Intelligence in Medical Practice: Enhancing
      Transparency, Accountability, and Responsible Artificial Intelligence use
T2  - Explainable AI in Clinical Practice: Methods, Applications, and
      Implementation
SP  - 69-89
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Elsevier
AB  - This chapter explores the pivotal role of explainable artificial
      intelligence (XAI) in transforming modern healthcare by bridging the gap
      between advanced computational models and human-centered clinical
      decision-making. While AI-driven tools have shown remarkable success in
      diagnostics, prognosis, and personalized treatment planning, their lack of
      transparency often raises concerns about trust, accountability, and
      ethical adoption. XAI seeks to address these challenges by making AI
      models more interpretable, thereby ensuring that healthcare professionals
      can understand, validate, and responsibly integrate algorithmic insights
      into practice. This chapter begins by outlining fundamental principles of
      explainability, discussing how techniques such as feature attribution,
      visualization, and rule-based models contribute to greater transparency.
      It then highlights the application of XAI across diverse healthcare
      domains, including medical imaging, predictive analytics, electronic
      health records, and drug discovery. Through real-world case studies, we
      examine how explainable models improve trust between clinicians and
      patients, enhance regulatory compliance, and mitigate biases inherent in
      black box systems. Finally, this chapter addresses practical dilemmas in
      implementing XAI, such as balancing accuracy with interpretability,
      safeguarding data privacy, and ensuring equitable outcomes. By promoting
      openness, responsibility, and conscientious implementation, XAI holds the
      promise of reshaping healthcare into a more transparent, ethical, and
      patient-centered domain. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
