VL  - 41
IS  - 15
SP  - 12399-12410
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH
AB  - This comprehensive review explores the transformative potential of
      visual-language foundation models (VL-FMs) in medical and clinical
      applications. By integrating deep visual perception with natural language
      understanding, these models enable context-aware interpretation of
      radiological, pathological, and ophthalmic images alongside clinical text.
      Technical advancements are analyzed, including transformer architectures,
      multi-modal fusion strategies, and knowledge integration frameworks. Case
      studies illustrate applications in disease diagnosis (e.g., diabetic
      retinopathy, lung cancer), image segmentation (e.g., brain tumors,
      vascular structures), and clinical decision support. Existing challenges
      such as data privacy, interpretability, and computational efficiency are
      discussed, alongside future directions for developing explainable and
      generalizable AI systems in precision medicine. © The Author(s), under
      exclusive licence to Springer-Verlag GmbH Germany, part of Springer Nature
      2025.
