TI  - X-FedAgriTwin: Privacy-preserving crop recommendation via Digital Twins
      and explainable federated learning
T2  - Inf. Softw. Technol.
JF  - Information and Software Technology
VL  - 196
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Elsevier B.V.
AB  - Context: Global food demand continues to rise amid increasing
      environmental and resource constraints, pressing agriculture to enhance
      productivity without compromising sustainability. Traditional data-driven
      farming approaches often face challenges related to data sensitivity,
      heterogeneous field conditions, and the lack of interpretability in
      decision-making systems. Objective: This study aims to design an
      intelligent, privacy-preserving, and explainable framework for crop
      recommendation that enhances both accuracy and trust in smart agriculture
      systems. Methods: We propose X-FedAgriTwin, a hybrid framework that
      integrates Digital Twin (DT) technology, Federated Learning (FL), and
      Explainable AI (XAI). The system enables real-time monitoring and
      decentralized model training using distributed sensor data while
      maintaining local data privacy. The predictive model is based on a
      multilayer perceptron (MLP) trained through federated learning across
      multiple nodes. Model interpretability is achieved through SHapley
      Additive exPlanations (SHAP), providing insights into feature
      contributions to crop recommendations. Results: Experimental evaluation
      demonstrates that the federated MLP model achieves 99.39% accuracy,
      outperforming centralized machine learning baselines. The model shows
      stable convergence within 30 communication rounds, confirming the
      efficiency of distributed training. SHAP analysis identifies potassium (K)
      and rainfall as the most influential features affecting crop
      recommendations. High K levels positively influence predictions, while low
      values reduce performance accuracy. Conclusion: The proposed X-FedAgriTwin
      framework effectively bridges predictive analytics, simulation, and
      explainability to support sustainable and data-secure precision
      agriculture. By ensuring transparency, continuous learning, and privacy
      preservation, it offers a scalable solution for real-world agricultural
      environments, fostering innovation and stakeholder confidence. © 2026
      Elsevier B.V. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data
      mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
