TI  - Applications in the electronic health record
T2  - Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning in Healthcare
SP  - 129-140
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Elsevier
AB  - The widespread adoption of electronic health records (EHRs) has created
      unprecedented opportunities for artificial intelligence (AI) and machine
      learning applications in healthcare. This chapter explores the secondary
      use of EHR data for research, predictive analytics, and clinical decision
      support within the framework of a learning health system. Key topics
      include data heterogeneity, integration of structured and unstructured
      data, and the role of natural language processing in leveraging clinical
      text. We review common AI methodologies, such as deep learning, and their
      applications in phenotyping, disease prediction, and outcome modeling.
      Additionally, we discuss interoperability challenges, data standards,
      federated networks, and privacy considerations. Finally, the chapter
      emphasizes explainable AI as a critical component for transparency, trust,
      and regulatory compliance in clinical environments. © 2026 Elsevier Inc.
      All rights reserved..
