AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI)in healthcare has
      revolutionized clinical decision-making, yetthe opacity ofmany AIsystems
      raises significant concerns about trust, accountability, and clinical
      adoption. This chapter examines explainable AI (XAI) and transparency in
      clinical decision support systems, exploring the critical balance between
      model performance and interpretability. We analyze various XAI techniques,
      from model-agnostic methods like LIME and SHAP to inherently interpretable
      approaches such as concept bottleneck models. The chapter discusses
      challenges including the evaluation of explanation quality,
      stakeholder-specific needs, and regulatory requirements. Copyright © 2027,
      IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or
