TI  - Hybrid Edge-Cloud Federated Learning Framework for Predictive Maintenance
      in Industrial IoT
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Industry 4.0 has enabled the use of Internet of Things (IoT) sensing and
      automated data analytics, making Predictive Maintenance (PdM) essential
      for identifying early equipment faults. However, many PdM systems rely on
      centralized cloud processing, which raises privacy concerns and struggles
      with heterogeneous Non-Independent and Identically Distributed (Non-IID)
      industrial data. To address these limitations, this paper introduces a
      Hybrid Edge-Cloud Federated Learning (FL) framework that performs local
      training on edge devices while aggregating global updates in the cloud.
      The proposed method is evaluated using the Case Western Reserve University
      (CWRU) bearing dataset, a widely-adopted benchmark in industrial fault
      diagnosis research. Results show that the federated model achieves
      accuracy comparable to centralized learning while preserving data privacy
      and maintaining robustness under Independent and Identically Distributed
      (IID) and Non-IID conditions. SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP)
      explainability further highlights the most influential features for fault
      classification, supporting transparent deployment in industrial
      environments. © 2025 IEEE.
