TI  - AI Applications in Ambulatory Medical Practice: Lessons from Digital
      Transformation
T2  - Advancements in Digital Health and Care: Empowering Healthcare Through
      Innovation, Strategies and Ethical Considerations
SP  - 95-106
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Springer Nature
AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into outpatient medical
      practice opens up new opportunities for improving diagnosis, patient
      management, and clinical decision-making processes. This chapter examines
      key applications of AI in outpatient care and draws lessons from previous
      digital transformation processes in healthcare. AI technologies such as
      machine learning, natural language processing, and predictive analytics
      enable more efficient patient data analysis, early detection of disease
      patterns, and personalized therapy recommendations. However, experience
      from digital transformation shows that technological innovation alone is
      not enough: successful implementation requires the adaptation of
      workflows, the training of medical staff, and the consideration of
      ethical, legal, and data protection aspects. Interoperability and
      user-friendly interfaces are crucial to ensuring acceptance and
      sustainability. In addition, case studies emphasize the importance of a
      step-by-step, evaluative approach that measures both clinical and
      organizational effects. Overall, the analysis makes it clear that AI must
      be viewed not only as a technical tool but also as an integral part of a
      comprehensive digital strategy. The findings provide practical
      recommendations for doctors, practice managers, and healthcare systems on
      how to use the potential of AI in outpatient care effectively and
      responsibly. © The Author(s) 2026.
