TY  - INPR
AU  - Hasan, Emon
TI  - Big Data-driven business process optimization: Enhancing decision-making
      through predictive analytics
T2  - Techrxiv
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025/10/7
AB  - The rapid growth of digital ecosystems has created an environment in which
      organizations generate and consume massive volumes of structured and
      unstructured data. Traditional business process management (BPM)
      approaches, while effective in well-defined workflows, struggle to capture
      the complexity, dynamism, and uncertainty inherent in today's business
      operations. Big Data analytics, when integrated with predictive modeling
      and machine learning, offers a transformative pathway to optimize business
      processes, reduce inefficiencies, and enhance decision-making at both
      strategic and operational levels. This paper explores a Big Data-driven
      framework for business process optimization that leverages advanced
      predictive analytics to anticipate process bottlenecks, forecast customer
      behavior, and recommend real-time adjustments. By incorporating event
      logs, transactional data, and external environmental factors into
      predictive models, the framework provides decision-makers with
      evidence-based insights that enhance agility and competitiveness. The
      study highlights how predictive models such as regression analysis,
      time-series forecasting, and neural networks can be applied to improve
      resource allocation, reduce operational costs, and minimize risks. The
      paper further demonstrates how organizations can transition from
      descriptive analytics, focused on past performance, to prescriptive
      analytics that actively supports decision-making in dynamic environments.
      Case studies in supply chain optimization, customer relationship
      management, and financial risk analysis are presented to validate the
      applicability of the approach. The findings indicate that Big Data-driven
      business process optimization not only improves efficiency but also drives
      innovation by uncovering latent patterns and opportunities that
      traditional methods overlook. The integration of predictive analytics into
      BPM ultimately empowers organizations to make faster, smarter, and more
      resilient decisions in a data-saturated economy.
