AB  - In this paper, a new real-world application problem, i.e., the vehicle
      fleet maintenance scheduling optimization problem, is defined and a
      specialized multi-objective evolutionary algorithm framework (grouping
      strategy, three vector chromosome and corresponding genetic operators) is
      proposed to solve the problem. State-of-the-art multi-objective
      evolutionary algorithms such as NSGA-III, SMS-EMOA, DI-MOEA are employed
      in the proposed algorithm framework to solve the problem, and their
      behavior is investigated. Although DI-MOEA is used the first time for a
      real-world application problem, its performance is better than other
      algorithms for some instances.
