TI  - QUANDO A IA PERGUNTA: TUTORIA SOCRÁTICA PARA FORTALECER A PRODUÇÃO ORAL
      UNIVERSITÁRIA
T2  - II MultiCientífica Brasil - Congresso Nacional Multidisciplinar
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026/7/10
PB  - Seven Congress
AB  - This article examines the enhancement of English as a foreign language
      learning at Universidad Politécnica de Querétaro in the context of
      generative artificial intelligence. The proposal addresses an
      institutional concern: students' insufficient functional command of
      B1-level oral production, communicative insecurity, assessment practices
      centered on grade-based accreditation, as well as the uncritical use of
      digital tools. Drawing on a qualitative, inductive approach supported by
      grounded theory and participant observation, the study proposes a
      technopedagogical strategy based on a Socratic tutor aligned with the
      Common European Framework of Reference for Languages. Through systematic
      oral micro-practices conducted inside and outside the classroom, the
      intervention seeks to foster discursive accuracy, self-repair, cognitive
      autonomy, and sustained participation. Artificial intelligence is thus
      conceived as a regulated pedagogical mediation capable of reconfiguring
      cultural practices of learning, assessment, and bilingual education in
      higher education.
