TI  - Intelligent Tutoring Systems from Symbolic AI to LLMs: A Critical Review
T2  - 2026 6th International Conference on Innovative Research in Applied
      Science, Engineering and Technology, IRASET 2026
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) represent for five decades an important
      deployment of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into the educational field,
      aiming to adapt and personalize learning. This paper provides a critical
      analysis of ITS evolution over five successive technological generations:
      Symbolic AI, cognitive architectures, web and probabilistic approaches,
      datadriven methods and the current era of Deep Learning (DL) and Large
      Language Models (LLMs). Our study presents four major paradigmatic
      transitions as well as persistent scientific challenges such as affective
      and motivational dimensions insufficiently integrated a trade-off between
      cognitive sophistication and scalability and limited dynamic modeling of
      individual trajectories. The integration of LLMs into multiagent
      architectures presents an opportunity to resolve these historically
      antagonistic dimensions. However, critical challenges remain concerning
      pedagogical reliability, the ability to justify decisions, multimodal
      fusion that improves results by using several data modalities and
      algorithmic fairness that avoids biases and discriminations. © 2026 IEEE.
