TI  - Intelligent Feedback Analytics: Hybrid LSTM-GPT Framework for Educational
      Improvement
T2  - International Conference on Intelligent and Innovative Practices in
      Engineering and Management, IIPEM 2025
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - In today's educational landscape, institutions are recognizing the
      importance of student feedback in improving teaching methods and learning
      experiences. However, traditional analysis methods, like manual reviews,
      surveys, and basic statistical tools, often fail to reveal the complex
      patterns within qualitative feedback data. To tackle this issue, this work
      introduces a new analytical approach using Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)
      algorithms for sentiment analysis. LSTM models can handle sequential and
      contextual data well, making them ideal for capturing the flow, tone, and
      deeper meanings in student responses. This helps us extract relevant
      insights into student emotions, concerns, and trends over time. By using
      LSTM, we move beyond superficial evaluations, leading to a better
      understanding of student sentiment. This helps educators and institutional
      leaders pinpoint areas for improvement and reinforce successful
      strategies. Besides LSTM, we also use a Generative Pre-trained Transformer
      (GPT) model to provide dynamic, personalized suggestions that support
      individual student development. GPT's language capabilities allow it to
      generate constructive, context-aware recommendations based on each
      student's feedback. By combining these two machine learning techniques,
      our system analyses student feedback with greater depth and accuracy while
      offering actionable, individualized recommendations. This intelligent
      approach improves both student outcomes and institutional effectiveness,
      making feedback a key tool in modern education. © 2025 IEEE.
