TI  - Research on a cross-cultural reflective education model empowered by
      generative artificial intelligence
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 International Conference on Big Data and
      Informatization Education, ICBDIE 2026
SP  - 147-156
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - Addressing the challenge of quantifying and promoting intercultural
      literacy and deep reflection in higher education institutions, this study
      proposes a generative AI-enabled model for intercultural reflection
      education. Based on the Bennett and Deardorff theoretical framework, the
      model integrates modules such as context generation, Socratic guided
      dialogue, multidimensional automatic assessment, and bias monitoring.
      Controlled experiments and performance tests were conducted in multiple
      schools and regions. Results show that the AI group significantly
      outperformed the control group in terms of reflection depth and
      intercultural sensitivity. Automatic scoring and expert review maintained
      high consistency, and the fairness and calibration indices of the main
      subgroups were within reasonable ranges. The system maintained acceptable
      latency and cost even under high concurrency. This study constructs a
      computable index system of reflection capabilities to verify the
      effectiveness of generative AI in supporting intercultural learning and
      reflection. An engineering implementation scheme for teaching platforms is
      proposed, providing a technical basis for large-scale, responsible
      application. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
