TI  - The Functional Architecture Design and Value Orientation of the
      Intelligent Tutoring System from the Perspective of Man-Machine
      Collaboration
SP  - 67-72
PY  - 2021
DA  - 2021
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
AB  - In the era of "artificial intelligence + education", personalized
      education based on man-machine collaboration has emerged. Based on the
      differences of learners and the implementation of personalized teaching,
      the functional architecture design of the "man-machine collaboration
      precision tutoring system"is proposed. The system architecture is divided
      into three layers: data resource layer, decision processing layer and
      interactive promotion layer. The data resource layer provides data
      recording and resource support, the decision processing layer plays the
      role of data diagnosis and learning analysis, and the interaction
      promotion layer realizes flexible interaction and grouping. Through
      collaboration and hierarchical interaction with teachers, a more idealized
      system can be constructed, which can integrate evidence analysis, timely
      feedback and personalized support. The value orientation of the system
      architecture is: teachers and students and intelligent systems expand time
      and space in collaborative activities, teachers and intelligent systems
      improve teaching in collaborative optimization, and students and
      intelligent systems enhance themselves in collaborative interaction. ©
      2021 ACM.
