TI  - Global Knowledge Mapping of Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Self-Regulated
      Learning in the 21st Century
SP  - 661-667
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - Artificial intelligence-enabled self-regulated learning represents an
      emerging interdisciplinary field that integrates computer science and
      educational psychology. To systematically examine the research status,
      hotspot topics, and developmental trends in this domain, this study
      employs bibliometric methods, utilizing CiteSpace and VOSviewer software
      to analyze 554 relevant publications from the Web of Science and Scopus
      databases spanning 2000-2025. The findings reveal: (1) Publication volume
      exhibits phased growth characteristics, with rapid expansion after 2021,
      reaching 135 articles in 2024, indicating a transition from marginal
      exploration to mainstream research focus; (2) Source journals demonstrate
      diversified characteristics, encompassing both educational technology and
      computer science journals, with educational journals showing more
      prominent academic impact; (3) The geographical distribution of research
      exhibits global characteristics, with China and the United States
      contributing the highest publication volumes, while countries such as the
      Netherlands, Germany, and Singapore demonstrate higher average citation
      rates, reflecting a divergence between publication volume and academic
      impact; (4) The field has established three major research clusters
      centered around Dragan Gašević, Roger Azevedo, and Inge Molenaar, focusing
      respectively on learning analytics, intelligent tutoring, and
      human-computer collaboration; (5) Research hotspots concentrate on three
      directions: intelligent learning support, data-driven analysis, and
      technology integration applications, constructing a comprehensive
      framework for the deep integration of AI and self-regulated learning; (6)
      The evolution of research frontiers has experienced three stages:
      technology foundation construction, theoretical integration development,
      and intelligent deep application, presenting a developmental logic from
      'technology adapting to education' to 'technology reshaping education.'
      This study provides a systematic knowledge mapping of the field, offering
      valuable reference for promoting the deep integration of AI technology and
      education. © 2025 IEEE.
