AB  - The article focuses on the question of how social processes of
      individualisation also affect the acquisition of foreign languages and in
      what form the development of hybrid learning concepts and environments
      follow these tendencies. Hybrid learning environments refer to specific
      networks of classroom learning and online-based learning that have
      previously been understood as blended learning. However, the emergence of
      new, intelligent assisted learning systems makes it necessary to redefine
      hybrid-learning environments. The article therefore deals with the
      specific features and functions of intelligent tutoring in foreign
      language teaching and deals with the learning technology requirements that
      these systems must meet in order to be able to find a new qualitative
      place in hybrid learning environments. The learning environment LSI.online
      is used as an example to illustrate the central function of intelligent
      assistance. © 2019, Danube Adria Association for Automation and
      Manufacturing, DAAAM. All rights reserved.
