PB  - Association for Computing Machinery, Inc
AB  - This paper presents a behavior-enhanced recommendation system for
      personalized English learning, designed to address the limitations of
      traditional collaborative filtering in educational environments. The
      proposed approach integrates user-based collaborative filtering with a
      multidimensional behavior profiling mechanism, enabling the system to
      capture both historical interaction data and real-time engagement
      patterns. A hybrid similarity function is constructed by combining Pearson
      correlation and behavior vector similarity, which significantly improves
      recommendation accuracy and contextual relevance. The system was validated
      using behavioral data from 1,000 university students collected during an
      academic semester. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed
      method outperforms baseline UserCF and content-based models in terms of
      Precision@5, Recall@5, F1-score, and MAP. The system maintains sub-second
      response times and exhibits strong scalability, making it suitable for
      deployment in large-scale digital learning platforms. This work
      contributes a modular, behavior-aware recommendation architecture that
      enhances both the technical performance and user experience of
      personalized learning systems. © 2025 Copyright held by the
      owner/author(s).
