TI  - Evaluation of Data Governance Frameworks for Trustworthy AI in Healthcare
SP  - 265-270
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - The evolution of Artificial intelligence (AI) has opened a new window for
      the public institutions to adopt automated work-process. Healthcare
      sectors have been facing consequences of digitalization due to their
      inclination over modern technologies for efficient handling of vast
      amounts of data that are being generated from healthcare systems
      comprising images, texts and administration reports. AI-driven solutions
      are beneficial for health systems in prediction of probable consequences
      and automation of work-process but this comes along with challenges in
      patient data security and trustworthiness of the automation models. The
      study provides an evaluation on the implementation of statistical analysis
      to determine how data governance practices are carried out in healthcare
      AI. The dataset used for performing the statistical analysis has been
      developed by collecting information across hospitals in the UK signifying
      realistic patient data. However, the name of the hospitals has been kept
      anonymous due to ethical and privacy concerns. Due to the fact that AI has
      occupied a prioritised position in the field of healthcare, it becomes
      necessary to develop concern on transparency and trust. The statistical
      analysis has been carried out using MS Excel to undergo analytics of
      datasets collected from Electronic Health Records (EHRs) and clinical data
      repositories . These analytical processes include the use of descriptive
      statistics to gain insights into samples and their impact on the data.
      Furthermore, t-tests have been carried out using ANOVA and Pivot tables
      and carts such that visualisation of the data can be done in terms of
      their quality testing. Findings from the study indicates that the use of
      data governance helps in protecting privacy and confidentiality of patient
      records stored across institutions offering services through AI.
