AB  - This chapter explores how ethical and human-centered artificial
      intelligence (Al) can transform teacher professional development (PD) by
      promoting personalized learning. reflective practice, and inclusive
      pedagogy. It examines the potential of Al tools such as intelligent
      tutoring systems, natural language processing, and learning analytics-to
      support adaptive learning, formative feedback, and collaborative
      professional communities. Addressing challenges of equity, cultural
      responsiveness, and data ethics, the chapter presents global case studies
      and a sustainability-aligned framework that links Al-driven PD to the UN
      Sustainable Development Goals (SDG 4 and SDG 10). Ultimately, it redefines
      teacher professionalism in the digital age, positioning educators as
      active agents of innovation and co-creators of equitable, future-ready
      education systems. Copyright © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
