TI  - Mapping the landscape of artificial intelligence and data literacy in
      education: A topic modelling and text mining approach
T2  - J. Res. Technol. Educ.
JF  - Journal of Research on Technology in Education
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) becomes pervasive in education, data
      literacy has emerged as a foundational competence in AI-mediated learning.
      Despite increasing research attention, the field remains fragmented, with
      limited longitudinal evidence on its thematic structure and evolution.
      Addressing this gap, this study presents a longitudinal analysis of AI and
      data literacy research from 2005 to 2025 using BERT-based and dynamic
      topic modeling. Twelve topic clusters were identified, revealing
      conceptual relationships, temporal trajectories, and citation patterns.
      Findings show rapid growth in topics related to intelligent tutoring
      systems, learning analytics, ethics, and evaluation-oriented data
      literacy, particularly following the rise of generative AI. Keyword
      network analysis indicates a shift from data mining and visualization
      toward AI-driven analytics and educational innovation. © 2026 ISTE+ASCD.
