AB  - As traditional Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITSs) are rule-based,
      inflexible, and opaque, these are unable to satisfy the increasing demand
      for individualized learning. These reduced student trust and engagement
      since these systems demonstrated a lack of responsiveness to the real
      behavior of students in the moment and were unable to defend the chosen
      teaching strategies. The study overcomes these limitations through study
      to customize a new AI teaching framework that employs explainable AI
      (SHAP), reinforcement learning for adaptive strategy selection, real-time
      processing for learner tracking, and large language models (LLMs). The
      proposed system has dynamic learner profile analysis to modify its
      instructional content and offers human-readable explanations of its
      modifications. It validates the proposed system performance and
      demonstrates that it exceeds baseline systems by 28.7% in accuracy,
      maintains high satisfaction levels (4.8/5), and retains users (85.6%). The
      model beats standard ITS in terms of accuracy, explainability, and user
      engagement metrics, confirming its capacity to deliver individualized,
      captivating, and reliable digital teaching experiences. © 2025 IEEE.
