TI  - SolveX A Plug and Play AI Tutor for Multi Variable Math Word Problems
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - The automated resolution of Mathematical Word Problems (MWPs) represents a
      central challenge in artificial intelligence, requiring the transformation
      of unstructured natural language into formally valid mathematical
      representations. Although recent Large Language Models (LLMs) have
      demonstrated strong performance in semantic understanding and
      text-to-equation generation, they remain susceptible to reasoning
      inconsistencies, hallucinated variables, and unreliable handling of
      multi-variable equation systems. The proposed system employs a structured
      orchestration strategy using LangChain and LangGraph to coordinate
      multiple specialized agents within a unified reasoning workflow. The
      pipeline consists of three key stages: (i) problem-type classification to
      enable adaptive prompt selection, (ii) structured extraction of variables
      and equations from natural language descriptions and (iii) deterministic
      equation consistency verification to ensure mathematical correctness. This
      architecture is a response to failure cases encountered in previous
      LLM-based methods, especially when dealing with complex problem classes
      featuring interdependent magnitudes. In addition to giving correct
      solutions, SolveX also provides answers with coherent solution step by
      step so as to improve transparency and educational value. We show that
      separating linguistic interpretation from verification-driven reasoning
      achieves 87% accuracy-8 points higher than GPT-4-while improving
      robustness and explainability over end-to-end generative baselines. © 2026
      IEEE.
