TI  - Human-like Mathematical Problem-Solving Brain for K-12 Education
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - This paper presents an interpretable intelligent tutoring system designed
      for algebraic problem-solving in K-12 education. By simulating students'
      cognitive processes, we propose a machine learning-based solution
      framework capable of automatically identifying multiple solution
      strategies and selecting optimal paths through feasibility analysis. We
      systematically evaluate three classifier architectures: a traditional SVM,
      a deep learningbased TextCNN, and a transformer-based BERT model.
      Comprehensive experiments on the Math23K and Ape210K datasets show that
      our BERT-enhanced system achieves a superior classification accuracy of
      86.65% while maintaining computational efficiency. The proposed
      architecture offers three key innovations: (1) a state-transition model
      for stepwise problem-solving, (2) a hybrid approach combining explicit and
      implicit condition handling, and (3) interpretable decision paths that
      mimic human reasoning. This work establishes a practical technical
      framework for AIassisted mathematics education, effectively balancing
      performance with pedagogical transparency. © 2025 IEEE.
