AU  - Zeer, Murad
TI  - The Role of AI in Enhancing Student Engagement and Motivation Through
      Personalized Learning
SP  - 69-74
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - As education shifts toward meeting each student's unique needs, artificial
      intelligence (AI) is stepping in as a game-changer to keep students
      engaged and excited about learning through personalized approaches. This
      paper dives into how AI can shake up education by crafting learning
      experiences that fit each student's strengths, struggles, and interests.
      With smart algorithms and tutoring systems, AI gives students feedback on
      the spot, tweaks lessons as they go, and even guesses what they'll need to
      learn next - making the whole process feel more lively and responsive.
      Plus, it throws in game-like features and adjusts to different learning
      styles, which can make lessons a lot more fun, especially for students who
      don't fit the usual mold or pace. That said, bringing AI into classrooms
      isn't all smooth sailing. There are real worries about keeping student
      info private, ensuring the tech plays fair for everyone, and making sure
      all kids - no matter where they come from - can actually use it. By
      digging into the latest research and real-life examples, this paper sheds
      light on both the cool possibilities and the tricky challenges of AI in
      personalized learning. It also tosses out some practical tips for teachers
      and tech folks on how to use AI in a way that's thoughtful and
      responsible, while pointing to a few ideas for future studies to crank up
      student motivation even more. In the end, it's all about showing how AI
      could not only help kids do better in school but also spark a love for
      learning that sticks with them for life. © 2025 IEEE.
