TI  - RL-Tutor: Combining Reinforcement Learning and Explainability for Adaptive
      Feedback Timing in Collaborative Learning
SP  - 1328-1335
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Collaborative learning platforms require timely, adaptive feedback to
      maintain engagement and participation equity. Current systems rely on
      static threshold-based rules that cannot learn optimal intervention timing
      or explain their decisions to users. We propose RL-Tutor, a conceptual
      framework combining reinforcement learning (RL) for adaptive feedback
      policy optimization with explainable AI (XAI) for transparent intervention
      justification. Our Q-Learning formulation learns when to intervene based
      on real-time behavioral signals (participation balance, engagement trends,
      task progress), while a templatebased XAI layer generates natural language
      explanations revealing the rationale behind each decision. Through
      illustrative synthetic scenarios, we demonstrate the proof-of-concept for
      how RL-Tutor could adapt intervention timing to group dynamics and provide
      transparent explanations that clarify system reasoning. This work
      contributes (1) an RL formulation (MDP and Qlearning instantiation) for
      collaborative feedback timing, (2) a lightweight XAI mechanism for
      pedagogical contexts, and (3) illustrative demonstration of the conceptual
      approach through representative scenarios. © 2026 IEEE.
