AU  - Ramaprasad, Jaya
TI  - Prism: Real-time Cognitive Tracking with Frictional AI
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - Prism is an AI-powered learning companion that treats every user query as
      an opportunity for structured cognitive engagement. Rather than provide an
      immediate friction-free response, it follows up with probing nudges to
      prompt the user to think more deeply about their question. These targeted
      Socratic follow-up questions create an interactive forum. A companion
      real-time dashboard - built on a proprietary cognitive framework mapping
      critical thinking dimensions to Explainable AI (XAI) categories (informed
      by related work on question-driven reflection in machine-assisted
      decision-making [1]) - scores each user's reasoning profile across four
      practitioner archetypes and surfaces nudges toward cognitive moves they
      have not yet made. The system is designed as a deliberate
      "frictional"intervention - slowing down the information-retrieval impulse
      to foster genuine epistemic engagement. Prism addresses the conference
      theme of Flow-Fun-Friction by demonstrating how productive friction in
      human-AI interaction can support professional learning and resistance to
      over-reliance on AI. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
