AU  - Rajagukguk, Sabar Aritonang
TI  - EduTransformer: A Multi-Modal Deep Learning Framework for Real-Time
      Personalized Learning Path Generation in Digital Education Platforms
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - The one-size-fits-all approach in traditional education systems fails to
      address individual learning needs, resulting in suboptimal outcomes for
      over 40% of students globally. This paper presents EduTransformer, a novel
      multi-modal deep learning framework that generates personalized learning
      paths in real-time by analyzing behavioral patterns, performance metrics,
      and content interactions. Our framework employs a transformer-based
      architecture with cross-attention mechanisms to fuse multiple data
      modalities, including clickstream data, assessment scores, and temporal
      learning patterns. We evaluate EduTransformer on a dataset comprising
      19,350 interactions from 387 students across diverse educational contexts.
      Experimental results demonstrate significant improvements: 32% increase in
      learning outcomes, 45% reduction in time-to-mastery, and 73% improvement
      in course completion rates compared to traditional learning management
      systems. The framework achieves 89% accuracy in next-content prediction
      and 94% precision in knowledge gap detection. Our contributions include:
      (1) the first transformer-based architecture for real-time educational
      personalization, (2) a novel multi-objective optimization approach
      balancing challenge and success, and (3) an explainable AI module
      providing interpretable recommendations for educators. This work advances
      intelligent tutoring systems and supports sustainable development goals in
      quality education. © 2025 IEEE.
