TI  - An Explainable Human-Centered Federated Generative Intelligent Tutoring
      System for Sustainable Education
SP  - 2065-2073
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITSs) play a vital role in sustainable
      education by enabling adaptive and personalized learning. However, current
      ITS systems have limited explainability, low level of personalization,
      privacy issues and lack of real-time adaptation of the learner. The
      majority of existing systems are based on traditional machine learning
      models that are not able to adequately model complex behaviour and
      interactions of learners. This paper presents a Federated Learning (FL)
      based Human-Centered Federated Generative Intelligent Tutoring System
      (HFG-ITS), which combines Federated Learning (FL), Transformer based
      Generative AI (GPT), Reinforcement Learning (RL), Knowledge Graphs (KG),
      and Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) to address these challenges.
      The proposed framework is based on the principles of decentralized
      training, generating dynamic personalized learning paths and adaptive
      interventions, while maintaining the privacy of the learner. Improved
      transparency and instructor trust is gained by incorporating SHAP-based
      explainability. Experimental testing on online educational datasets shows
      that the results are better with 98.74% accuracy, 98.21% F1-score and a
      34.6% decrease in dropout prediction error compared to the existing ITS
      models. Moreover, the engagement of learners was enhanced by 29.4%,
      indicating the efficacy of the framework to create secure, explainable and
      scalable sustainable learning environments. © 2026 IEEE.
