TI  - AI-Powered Personalization for Enhancing Student Engagement in E-Learning
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - E-learning has opened up a lot of choices for easy and flexible education
      in today's fast-changing digital environment. But even though it has a lot
      of good points, many students still have trouble staying engaged. Generic
      course content, excessive screen time, and not getting feedback right away
      are all things that might make students do poorly in school and lose
      interest. This study looks at how artificial intelligence (AI) may change
      that story. By adding AI-powered customization, we can make e-learning
      systems more flexible, motivating, and tailored to the needs of each
      student. We studied 120 students from three major online venues. We found
      that students were far more engaged, felt better, and did better when we
      employed technology like intelligent feedback systems, personalized
      learning paths, and real-time data monitoring. Along with a big decline in
      dropout rates, overall engagement scores went up. These findings show that
      AI is more than just a technical improvement; it is a transformative force
      that makes learning better and more focused on people. © 2025 IEEE.
