AB  - In the context of advances in information technology, which impact on
      several aspects of life in society, this article aims to analyze the
      processing and sharing of personal data by the Public Administration,
      under the justification of the need to prepare and implement public
      policies. The analysis will be performed considering the fundamental right
      to the protection of personal data and the protective archetype resulting
      from the new Brazilian legislation regarding data protection. The points
      raised will highlight incompatibilities of Decree No. 10,046/2019 with the
      Constitution of the Republic of 1988 and the General Data Protection Law
      (Law no. 13,709/2018).
