TI  - AI-DRIVEN PERSONALIZED EDUCATION SYSTEMS: ENHANCING ADAPTIVE LEARNING
      THROUGH INTELLIGENT TUTORING
T2  - Proc. Eng. Sci.
JF  - Proceedings on Engineering Sciences
VL  - 7
IS  - 4
SP  - 2819-2832
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Faculty of Engineering, University of Kragujevac
AB  - The diligent move to e-learning has ensured the relevance of sophisticated
      learning systems that can cater to each student. Most traditional
      e-learning systems still stick to rigid templates that do not take
      individual learning and engagement levels and comprehension skills into
      consideration. Therefore, these students are liable to suffer from lack of
      motivation, low retention, and poor learning outcomes. In an attempt to
      mitigate these shortcomings, this paper proposes an AI-enabled
      personalized education system that adjusts students’ learning experiences
      in real time by analyzing their behavior, performance, and preferences. To
      test the validity of AI powered education system, we carried out a vast
      number of real world experiments using e-learning data sets. Our research
      focused on the central KPIs, including learning retention, user
      engagement, and overall learning productivity, contrasting AI-assisted
      learning to conventional learned models. Our findings indicate that the
      proposed system achieved 30% improvement in retention and 25% increase in
      engagement, which means that these features surpass traditional measures.
      Additionally, the content adapted approach has also minimized drop-out
      rates among students, as the content was more in-tune with their abilities
      and learners’ interests. While the potential of AI systems in education is
      enormous, they Moreover, these technologies bring up important issues
      regarding data privacy, algorithmic bias, and an over dependence on
      AI-based instruction. To be able to trust intelligent tutoring systems, it
      is important to ensure fairness and transparency in AI generated
      recommendations. To address these issues, we use explainable AI approaches
      and privacy preserving techniques like federated learning, which enables
      decentralized model training without access to sensitive student
      information. © 2025 Published by Faculty of Engineeringg.
