TI  - Classrooms Without Borders: Charting Innovative Pathways for Artificial
      Intelligence in Education
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming and reshaping the educational
      domain. As educators seek innovative approaches to improve student
      outcomes, AI's capacity to tailor resources and predict performance makes
      it indispensable for classrooms. Existing research focuses on narrow
      aspects, overlooking a holistic perspective that embraces teacher training
      needs, ethical considerations, and policy frameworks. This review aims to
      investigate how AI-driven solutions can be effectively integrated into
      teaching. Using a narrative method, studies are synthesized to illustrate
      its successes and emerging gaps. While it can significantly enrich
      pedagogical processes, responsible implementation, stakeholder
      collaboration, and ethical awareness remain essential for sustained
      impact. Our findings reveal notable gains in personalization and
      efficiency yet underline persistent hurdles in data privacy, algorithmic
      bias, and teacher readiness. By emphasizing trends and shortfalls, this
      review contributes to a multidimensional understanding of AI's potential
      and harnessing it judiciously for a more equitable learning outcome. ©
      2025 IEEE.
