TI  - Design of Adaptive Training Control in Dispatcher Training Simulators
SP  - 1885-1891
PY  - 2023
DA  - 2023
AB  - With the expansion of power systems and the development of smart grids,
      power system operations become increasingly complex and critical, calling
      for skilled and experienced dispatchers. The dispatcher training simulator
      (DTS) has been widely used as an effective training tool for decades,
      providing a realistic simulation of the dispatching environment. Efforts
      have been made to improve the simulation of DTS, while there is a research
      gap in improving the training module of DTS. Currently, DTS does not
      consider trainees' learning states and preferences, and therefore cannot
      provide customized training services for different trainees, limiting its
      training effectiveness. Referring to learning analytics and adaptive
      learning systems, this paper investigates the training process control of
      DTS based on trainees' learning states. A data-driven adaptive training
      control framework is proposed, including three stages: learning state
      monitoring, learning state assessment, and learning process control. The
      presented adaptive training control framework allows the DTS system to
      provide personalized and targeted training services to dispatcher
      trainees, promoting the intelligence and automation of the DTS system. ©
      2023 IEEE.
