AU  - Lafham, Mohamed
AU  - Bachari, Essaid E L
TI  - Smart Tutoring Systems in Education 4.0: A Systematic Review
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - Education 4.0 is transforming learning by integrating artificial
      intelligence (AI), intelligent tutoring systems (ITS), and adaptive
      learning technologies. This systematic review synthesizes twenty
      high-quality studies published between 2020 and 2025, focusing on how
      these tools reshape teaching and learning. Key technologies include large
      language models (LLMs), adaptive platforms, learning analytics, and
      AI-supported collaborative environments. The review identifies three major
      insights: (i) ITS and LLMs enhance learner motivation and performance,
      while supporting teachers with adaptive feedback; (ii) persistent gaps
      remain in long-term evaluation, ethical design, and implementation in
      under-resourced settings; (iii) most studies are limited to short-term or
      well-resourced contexts, raising concerns about generalizability. To
      address these gaps, the review highlights the need for ethical AI
      principles, inclusive design, and systematic teacher training. The
      contributions of this work are threefold: (1) mapping recent trends and
      methodologies in ITS research, (2) identifying underexplored ethical and
      practical challenges, and (3) proposing directions for combining
      personalization with collaborative learning in Education 4.0. This
      synthesis provides actionable insights for researchers, educators, and
      policymakers seeking to leverage AI responsibly for equitable educational
      transformation. ©2025 IEEE.
