AU  - M, S
TI  - Privacy-Preserving Explainable AI Framework for Lung Disease Detection
      Using Multi-Agent Systems and Blockchain
SP  - 1-5
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - One of the major imperatives for the transition toward these technologies
      is their ability to diagnose diseases automatically and more accurately.
      As a case in point, this has significantly revolutionized the diagnosis of
      lung diseases by using Artificial Intelligence (AI) for analyzing lung CT
      images. However, the deployment of such systems in the real world is still
      problematic with issues such as the privacy and security of data, the non,
      interpretability of these methods, and the limited clinical trust they
      enjoy. This paper therefore focuses on a privacy, preserving and
      explainable $e$, healthcare solution that supports lung disease diagnosis
      through the integration of multi, agent systems, interpretable machine
      learning, explainable deep learning, and blockchain technology. The
      proposed framework leverages the distributed multi, agent architecture
      with the Role, Based Access Control (RBAC) mechanism working with Data
      Custodian Agents (DCA) who hold and restrict access to the data, Privacy
      Auditor Agents (PAA) who examine the sharing process and consent,
      Inference Agents (IA) who process the data and generate models, Decision
      Enforcement Agents (DEA) who authorize the actions of the agents based on
      the smart contracts, and Blockchain Agents (BCA) who record all events in
      the chain of blocks in a transparent and immutable way. Meanwhile, in the
      Random Forest classifier model that analyzes structured patient data, the
      feature importance plot is used for providing transparent explanations for
      the most influential variables. The CNN model and its state, of, the, art
      architecture such as ResNet, VGG, or DenseNet can be exploited to extract
      the representative features of the lung CT images. One of the major
      bottlenecks deep neural network, based methods suffer from is their black,
      box nature, which means the model gives the results without providing
      sufficient reasons for them. Among numerous techniques, the Grad CAM is
      well known for producing detailed heatmaps that reflect the most important
      regions in the image that are employed by the model to make the
      prediction. Besides that, the implementation of a lightweight private
      blockchain with the SHA, 256 cryptographic hash function guarantees the
      integrity, accountability, and non, repudiation of the diagnostic records
      without the need for a trusted intermediary.
