AB  - This book offers an in-depth exploration of explainable learner models,
      presenting theoretical foundations and practical applications in the
      context of educational AI. It aims to provide readers with a comprehensive
      understanding of how these models can enhance adaptive learning systems.
      Chapters cover a wide range of topics, including the development and
      optimization of explainable learner models, the integration of these
      models into adaptive learning systems, and their implications for
      educational equity. It also discusses the latest advancements in AI
      explainability techniques, such as pre-hoc and post-hoc explainability,
      and their application in intelligent tutoring systems. Lastly, the book
      provides practical examples and case studies to illustrate how explainable
      learner models can be implemented in real-world educational settings. This
      book is an essential resource for researchers, educators, and
      practitioners interested in the intersection of AI and education. It
      offers valuable insights for those looking to integrate explainable AI
      into their educational practices, as well as for policymakers focused on
      promoting equitable and transparent learning environments. © 2025 Bo
      Jiang.
