AB  - Artificial intelligence in education is now being talked about in the
      context of personalization, conversational support, automated assessment,
      and institutional adoption, but the entrepreneurial and cybersecurity
      aspects of the developments are not fully incorporated. Relying on a
      hierarchical narrative analysis of thirty-seven sources on the subject
      that use domains, this chapter combines learning analytics, adaptive
      gamification, domain-focused knowledge graphs, chatbot mediation,
      micro-credentialing, and governance constraints to form a single
      pedagogical structure. successful tutoring of cybersecurity
      entrepreneurship ought to be artifact-based, contextualized to startups,
      legally conscious, and analytics-intensive since startups and early-stage
      teams ought to be trained to prioritize threats, justify controls,
      communicate residual risk, and productize trust in harsh conditions of
      uncertainty. As a result, an assessment logic based on rubrics, and an
      implementation roadmap are elaborated to facilitate human-assisted,
      AI-enhancedlearningofcyberrisksintechnologystartups. © 2026 by IGI Global
      Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved. No part of this publication
