TI  - Review on the Design and Development of an Intelligent Pedagogical
      Assistant for Predictive Analysis of Academic Dropout
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
PB  - Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.
AB  - Academic dropout is a significant problem for higher education
      institutions, having an impact on student success and institutional
      performance. New developments in Artificial Intelligence and Learning
      Analytics have created opportunities to identify risk at an early stage
      and provide individualized learning. This paper is a systematic literature
      review undertaken with the PRISMA guidelines to examine existing
      intelligent pedagogical assistant research in the predictive study on
      academic dropout. The review looks at methodological tendencies, type of
      data, predictors, explainability strategies, and incorporation methods in
      smart tutoring systems. This work, based on the analysis of the selected
      works, suggests a systematic taxonomy and determines important research
      lacunae, such as inadequate incorporation of conversational AI, scientific
      grounding mechanisms, and fragmented educator-oriented dashboards. The
      results stress the necessity of integrated, learner-centered frameworks
      that combine predictive modeling, intelligible analytics, conversational
      intelligence, and governed knowledge recall to assist in proactive dropout
      prevention at higher education. © 2026 IEEE.
