AB  - India's National Education Policy 2020 integrates Artificial Intelligence
      to address educational disparities across heterogeneous contexts—rural-
      urban divides, resource- constrained government schools, and
      technologically advanced academies. The chapter employs qualitative policy
      examination, institutional readiness assessments, and critical synthesis
      of empirical research on intelligent tutoring systems and learning
      analytics within Indian educational ecosystems. Analysis reveals AI's
      multifaceted potential: personalised learning pathways, augmented teacher
      capacity in under- resourced contexts, and equitable access in
      geographically dispersed communities. The 2026- 27 mandatory AI curriculum
      presents developmental opportunities; success requires substantial
      investment in teacher preparation and critical AI literacy. Realising
      transformative potential demands balanced integration of technological
      innovation with institutional capacity building, teacher empowerment, and
      transparent governance, prioritising educational equity and resource
      allocation. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights
      reserved.
