AB  - The current study introduces a model for measuring student diligence using
      online behaviors during intelligent tutoring system use. This model is
      validated using a full academic year dataset to test its predictive
      validity against long-Term academic outcomes including end-of-year grades
      and total work completed by the end of the year. The model is additionally
      validated for robustness to time-sample length as well as data sampling
      frequency. While the model is shown to be predictive and robust to
      time-sample length, the results are inconclusive for robustness in data
      sampling frequency. Implications for research on interventions, and
      understanding the influence of self-control, motivation, metacognition,
      and cognition are discussed. © 2017 ACM.
