AB  - Individualized treatment, data-driven decision-making, and improved
      diagnosis are the hallmarks of the technology-driven new era in health
      care. But these developments pose a few challenges as well, including the
      need for dependable infrastructure, the ethical application of AI, and the
      efficient application of big data. Four main areas are this paper:
      infrastructure perspectives, big data analytics, model-guided medicine,
      and the challenges of artificial intelligence in health care. Every
      component is backed up with the evidence-based analysis and mathematical
      support. We offer a synthesized and distinguished perspective on how to
      get over current obstacles and improve health care delivery by drawing on
      insights from top literature. The study ends with a comparative table and
      future scope that highlights new possibilities and systemic changes that
      are needed.
