TI  - AI-Enhanced Entrepreneurial Education: Personalizing Learning Pathways
T2  - Decision Making, Learning, and Collaboration in AI-Driven Entrepreneurship
SP  - 75-88
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) is reshaping entrepreneurial education by
      enabling per¬sonalized learning pathways that cater to individual learner
      needs, preferences, and competencies. This chapter explores how AI
      technologies—such as adaptive learning systems, intelligent tutoring,
      generative AI, and learning analytics—facilitate customized instruction,
      real-time feedback, and experiential learning opportunities. Drawing on
      constructivist, experiential, and cognitive learning theories, the chapter
      examines the design and implementation of personalized pathways,
      highlighting case studies that demonstrate improved learner engagement,
      skill acquisition, and entrepreneurial decision-making. It also addresses
      key challenges, including data privacy, algorithmic bias, equity, and the
      balance between AI guidance and human mentorship. Finally, the chapter
      identifiesfuture directions for research and practice, emphasizing
      immersive technologies, predictive analytics, and ethical frameworks to
      enhance the effectiveness and inclusivity of entrepreneurial education. ©
      2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
