TI  - A Survey on AI Applications in the Open Classroom Approach
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - The open classroom approach emerged as a practical and adaptable learning
      environment that promotes not only student-centered learning but also the
      collaboration of students and modern technology. On the other hand,
      artificial intelligence (AI) has been very dynamic in the education
      industry, serving as a facilitator of smart tutoring systems, adaptive
      learning platforms, learning analytics, and virtual assistance. This
      survey study delves deeper into the area of AI technologies and the open
      classroom paradigm. AI-powered systems like intelligent tutoring systems,
      adaptive learning platforms, and learning analytics tools have envisioned,
      fostered, and realized the goals of open classrooms, such as
      personalization, engagement, and self-regulated learning. In addition, the
      article describes the latest AI solutions that have been tested and
      evaluated in open classrooms, accentuates the features that they share,
      and identifies the persistent problems that arise from privacy protection
      and technology constraints. It is in the development of future research
      directions that the fusion of AI and open classrooms is proposed as the
      best approach to work on personalized learning paths, the integration of
      multimodal data, and finally, human-AI collaboration in education. © 2025
      IEEE.
