TI  - AI-Powered Adaptive E-Learning to Improve Accessibility for Diverse
      Learner Demographics
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2025
AB  - The increasing global adoption of e-learning technologies has opened new
      avenues for flexible, scalable, and remote education. However, significant
      disparities in accessibility and learner engagement persist, particularly
      among users from diverse demographic backgrounds with varying levels of
      cognitive ability, digital literacy, and technological access. This
      research explores the development and application of AI-powered adaptive
      e-learning platforms designed to address these challenges by delivering
      personalized and inclusive learning experiences. The proposed system
      integrates machine learning algorithms and real-time analytics to tailor
      instructional content, interface interactions, and learning pathways
      according to individual learner profiles. Key features include content
      adaptation based on user behavior, accessibility enhancements for users
      with disabilities, and bandwidth-aware resource delivery for
      under-connected environments. A mixed-methods evaluation involving
      usability testing, learning analytics, and user satisfaction surveys
      demonstrates that adaptive personalization significantly improves learning
      outcomes, engagement, and perceived accessibility. The study contributes
      to the growing field of AI in education by offering a framework for
      inclusive digital learning environments and presents implications for
      future research in educational technology, digital equity, and intelligent
      tutoring systems. © 2025 IEEE.
