AB  - Integration of Artificial Intelligence in learning has demonstrated a
      tremors in the way of teaching and learning way of life. First to jump
      onto this bandwagon are AI-driven learning systems, which present
      process-driven instruction that is personalized based on each user,
      adaptive, and informed by data. In this paper we Voronezhskiy. Interop
      assembly-based probes are also presented to compare Luo and Latex
      performances on making comparison. AI of things assists in aiding the
      adaptive learning platforms to apply machine learning algorithms, natural
      language processing, predictive analytics to assess the student
      performance, identify learning gaps, and provide personalized content. In
      fact, these systems are seeking to replace a human tutor by responding to
      feedback in real time, critically and responsively evaluating content and
      intelligently adjusting it. AI platforms desire to make the learning
      session personalized They insist that customizing to the learner and
      learners pace and style of study will help in making the process more
      engaged, memorable and successful. Universal AI: AI-enhanced platforms
      have too varied an interface based on infrastructure, digital literacy,
      application in learning and education, and economic inequality. These
      platforms have been as well resourced settings. An intelligent tutoring
