AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into digital education
      marks a ma-jor shift in pedagogy, learner engagement, and institutional
      functions. Al-driven systemssuch as intelligent tutoring, adaptive
      learning, and learning analytics are transforming how knowledge is
      delivered and assessed. This chapter explores Al's role in creating
      adaptive learning environments, supporting both cognitive and emotional
      assessment, and improving institutional efficiency through automation.
      Global platforms including Squirrel AI, Carnegie Learning, Duolingo, and
      DIKSHA are examined. The chapter also addresses ethical, technical, and
      infrastructural challenges, including privacy, algorithmic bias, and the
      digital divide. It synthesizes current literature and promotes comparative
      perspectives to support ethical, equita-ble, and learner-centered Al
      integration, while outlining key Al tools for education, research,
      paraphrasing, and collaboration. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific
      Publishing. All rights reserved.
